\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Succumb to U.S. dollar strength. \b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2003\par 11:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  finally\par yielded ground to a rising U.S. dollar on Tuesday, as the\par optimism about a U.S. recovery overshadowed the region's\par surging stock markets and foreign investment inflows.\par     Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  contributed to the dollar strength\par when the head of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  department told Reuters\par that now was a good time to buy U.S. Treasuries, and said the\par euro was too expensive.\par     Traders said with the euro at four-month lows, the yen\par   giving up resistance and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies of\par regional central banks, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were bound to feel\par some pressure.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar        slipped to the weaker side of\par 1.75, making it among the weakest regional on the day.\par     The Thai baht        shrugged off repeated comments from\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and other policymakers that its strength was\par not hurting exports and therefore not worrying, and fell.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japan's Nikkei average         rose to its highest level in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 13 months, the Korean stock market  hit an 11-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high, and Thai stocks  reached their highest in over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par four years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  ended onshore trade almost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unchanged, paring gains as stocks ended lower and amid talk of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to pull the Korean won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   down.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stock market  was also in negative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par territory on Tuesday afternoon, having hit 13-month highs the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous day, as the impact of a government plan to cut pension\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par costs borne by employers seemed to be wearing off.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "That the government has employed such drastic measures on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the fiscal front, the risk is that some sort of Sing dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakness will also be employed as added cushions," United\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overseas Bank said in their commentary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RUPIAH FIRM, PESO WEAK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  was the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par region to gain substantially, rallying in relief after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par National Day holiday weekend passed without any militant\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attacks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso fell in early trade to 55.15, a five-month low,\par and stayed weak as politics remained the overriding concern.\par     Traders said they suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had sold some\par dollars to stop it falling to 55.16, the low struck in March.\par     Allegations about the business dealings of President Gloria\par Macapagal's Arroyo husband, made by an opposition senator in a\par privileged speech on Monday, kept Philippine markets unsettled.\par     "The market seems to be reacting to today's headlines plus\par weaker regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . We're watching the market," \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor Amando Tetangco told Reuters.\par     On Tuesday, the Philippines reported its first monthly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade surplus for this year in June, owing to increased demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for its electronics exports, but it offered little comfort to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Political and policy continuity concerns have been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heightened after a failed mutiny on July 27 and a recent court\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par order suspending \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a year over the closure of a commercial bank. The suspension\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cannot be enforced until the appeals are exhausted.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0836 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.55       119.23         -0.27\par  Sing dlr      1.7515       1.7470         -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.353       34.358         +0.01\par  Korean won   1179.10      1178.20         -0.08\par  Baht           41.64        41.60         -0.10\par  Peso           55.12        55.09         -0.05\par  Rupiah       8473.00      8496.00         +0.27\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.55       118.74         -0.68