\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Pare early gains, peso struggles. \b0\par\par\uc2 695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2003\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso struggled\par to make a convincing move from five-month lows on Wednesday,\par and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared early gains after the Japanese\par yen eased to the weaker side of 119 per U.S. dollar.\par     The peso ended local trade with some gains, but the fear\par of\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a factor after it had slipped\par towards Tuesday's low of 54.97 per dollar in morning trade.\par     Dealers said the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision to leave\par key rates unchanged, as had been expected, had little impact on\par regionals outside its influence on the yen .\par     The South Korean won                   hit a one-month high\par of 1,177.2 in early trade but then retreated to near the lows\par it saw on Monday. The Taiwan dollar  touched a two-week\par high of 34.357 per dollar, before also pulling back. Traders in\par both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar       , Thai baht        and the\par Indonesian rupiah  were all a touch lower, but within\par familiar ranges.\par     "The Fed's decision to leave rates unchanged hardly made\par markets excited. As such, activity on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  front remains\par dull," said Thio Chin Lo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP\par Paribas.\par     She said the summer holiday season in the United States was\par keeping markets lacklustre, although key U.S. data this week --\par including retail sales, business inventories and import prices\par -- could inspire some action.\par     The peso hit a low of 54.945 in morning trade, just shy of\par Tuesday's five-month low, before wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par prompted traders to unwind long dollar positions.\par     Dealers in Manila said the seasonal rise in dollar demand\par for imports in August and September, and political worries as\par the trial of one of the leaders of last month's failed mutiny\par began, were weighing down the peso.\par     Traders suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had sold dollars just\par ahead of the local close on Tuesday, and expect that it would\par continue to defend 55 per dollar.\par     "There was no activity by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but corporates\par are still in the market for dollars, although demand seems to\par taper off as we approach 54.95," said chief dealer of a local\par bank.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        fell from Tuesday' highs\par around 8,500 per dollar, and dealers in Jakarta said security\par worries ahead of the Indonesia's national day on Sunday could\par pull it down further.\par     Good two-way interest kept the Sing dollar in a\par 1.7540-1.7580 range. Dealers said some long-term players were\par spotted unloading U.S. dollars, but that was easily absorbed by\par the market.\par     The baht sat at 41.80 per dollar, with support from\par equity-related inflows countered by wariness of possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar sales aimed at keeping exports competitive.\par  \par     The Bank of Thailand capped the baht's strength in June and\par July, when it was mostly on the strong side of 41.80.\par     Equity inflows helped the Korean won, but sentiment was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cooled by data showing the unemployment rate in July was steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at a 22-month peak of 3.6 percent. Some dollar demand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par importers and wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , seen when the won was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at similar levels in July, also tempered the gains. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0812 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.11       118.66         -0.38\par  Sing dlr      1.7568       1.7551         -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.385       34.382          0.00\par  Korean won   1179.70      1178.70         -0.08\par  Baht           41.79        41.78         -0.02\par  Peso           54.83        54.89         +0.11\par  Rupiah       8544.00      8530.00         -0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.11       118.74         -0.31\par  Sing dlr      1.7568       1.7341         -1.29\par  Taiwan dlr    34.385       34.753         +1.08\par  Korean won   1179.70      1185.80         +0.52\par  Baht           41.79        43.08         +3.09\par  Peso           54.83        53.38         -2.64\par  Rupiah       8544.00      8940.00         +4.63.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030813dz8d00hg3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
