\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bombing impact eases, risks linger. \b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2003\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah managed\par to post some gains on Wednesday as Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trimmed the\par losses they sustained after bombing of a Jakarta hotel, but\par worries about regional security kept markets cautious.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were still weaker from the start of the week as\par worries over the U.S. economy and volatile asset markets, the\par sustainability of foreign equity inflows into the region, and\par the threat of more attacks remained.\par     The rupiah        fell as far as 8,720 per dollar in\par morning deals, near the three-month low of 8,725 low struck two\par weeks ago, in a sell-off triggered by Tuesday's bombing of\par Jakarta's JW Marriott Hotel, which claimed up to 16 lives.\par     It rallied over 100 rupiah, and stayed there, after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's senior deputy governor told Reuters that the\par bank would try to limit the impact of the bombing on the\par rupiah, a sign it was ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to check the fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Forwards on the rupiah betrayed some of the nervousness in\par the market. The three-month dollar premium rose to 182 points,\par last seen in late May and sharply up from 165 on Tuesday.\par     Analysts said the bearishness following the bombing would\par linger for some days. More importantly, the incident gave\par markets an excuse to offload Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings built up\par on hopes of stronger growth and foreign investment inflows,\par they said.\par     "The tone is a little bit on the soft side, firstly as we\par may have seen a peak in the equity capital inflows for a little\par while at least," said David Simmonds, markets strategist at the\par Royal Bank of Scotland.\par     "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have not been allowed to go any stronger\par over the last couple of weeks, on the back of the relative\par growth optimism and the equity capital inflows, at some point\par there will be periods of reappraisal and position-squaring."\par     "The dip in the equity inflows combined with events in\par southeast Asia and Jakarta may provide some impetus to the\par position squaring," Simmonds said.\par     The Thai baht       , perceived to be a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  backed by\par strong fundamentals and rising foreign interest, was steady at\par 42.04/08.\par     Analysts said this bout of weakness gave central banks some\par respite from having to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to contain \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par appreciation, particularly in Korea, Taiwan and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Definitely Singapore is one candidate that would not be\par averse to further Sing dollar weakening, so long as it remains\par within their policy band," said Claudio Piron, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with Standard Chartered Bank.\par     The Singapore dollar        was sold heavily in early\par trade, but stopped short of Tuesday's three-month lows around\par 1.7668 before cutting its losses.\par     Foreigners were net sellers of Korean and Taiwan stocks on\par Wednesday. Stock markets in Korea and Taiwan fell, partly in\par line with the decline on Wall Street.\par  \par     The Taiwan dollar          ended the day just fractionally\par higher and the won  managed modest gains.\par     The bombing also highlighted the vulnerability of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippine peso , which has been under pressure after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par failed mutiny on July 27 and the subsequent risks of political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par instability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso, which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defended ahead of the key 55 per dollar level, was range-bound\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday and ended slightly higher in onshore deals.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0810 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.96       120.44         +0.40\par  Sing dlr      1.7618       1.7655         +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.446       34.466         +0.06\par  Korean won   1184.60      1187.90         +0.28\par  Baht           42.06        42.06          0.00\par  Peso           54.79        54.82         +0.05\par  Rupiah       8585.00      8610.00         +0.29\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.96       118.74         -1.02\par  Sing dlr      1.7618       1.7341         -1.57\par  Taiwan dlr    34.446       34.753         +0.89\par  Korean won   1184.60      1185.80         +0.10\par  Baht           42.06        43.08         +2.43\par  Peso           54.79        53.38         -2.57\par  Rupiah       8585.00      8940.00         +4.14 ((Reporting by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vidya Ranganathan, editing by John Mair;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3090)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030806dz8600hqy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
