\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won hits 1-mth lows, others mixed. \b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2003\par 06:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell to a\par one-month low on Tuesday, helped along by authorities, while\par the Philippine peso and Indonesian rupiah resisted the downward\par pressure seen in other Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The won                  was sold down to 1,188.4 per U.S.\par dollar, its weakest since July 2, after dealers said they\par spotted dollar purchases from financial authorities apparently\par aimed at soaking up supply of dollars from equity-related\par inflows.\par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in\par Singapore, said Korean authorities had been buying dollars\par since Friday and given the yen's weakness on Tuesday those\par purchases might have picked up.\par     Despite the won's losses, it remained on the strong side of\par 10 on the yen-won cross , where it has been since\par mid-July.\par     "We are still in an environment where central banks in Asia\par are reluctant to see their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate," Malcolm\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He said the aversion to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength stemmed from\par worries about exports growth and domestic monetary conditions.\par     "We think this is going to change, but picking the timing\par is like taking a shot in the dark at the moment," he said,\par adding confidence of a global recovery would lead to the shift.\par     The Philippine peso        edged slightly higher to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 54.75 per dollar, from Monday's local close of 54.80, amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has raised its monitoring of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar purchases by banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso fell to a four-month lows just shy of the 55 per\par dollar level last week after a failed mutiny on July 27.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was also off its recent lows,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the market seen consolidating after last month's volatile\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moves when it fell to three-month lows and provoked aggressive\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities to prop it up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar  was slightly easier on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker side of 1.76 per U.S. dollar. Dealers said the downside\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was likely to be limited after data showed an expansion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturing sector for the second straight month in July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Purchasing Managers' Index climbed 0.6 points in July\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to an eight-month high of 51.4 percent fuelled by new export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par orders, expanding employment and inventories.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht       , tracking moves in the Singapore\par dollar and the yen, eased closer to 42 per dollar.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0351 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.34       119.88         -0.38\par  Sing dlr      1.7624       1.7590 