\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Further rupiah losses,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2003\par 05:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 24 (Reuters) - The nose-diving Indonesian\par rupiah overwhelmed Asian trading once again on Thursday morning\par as traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  persisted with U.S. dollar\par sales to try to stem its losses as it slumped to three-month\par lows.\par     The rupiah        hit 8,725 per dollar, taking its losses\par in the past week to over five percent, before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said. There was a sympathetic drop in the\par Philippine peso  as fears foreign investors would flee\par Asia's two highest-yielding markets en masse weighed. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  there \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  verbally, predicting the peso\par would soon rally.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were inching higher, indifferent to\par the U.S. dollar's fall on weak stock markets and Federal\par Reserve Governor Ben Bernanke's remarks that U.S. rates could\par be cut further.\par    Part of Asia's muted reaction reflected market wariness\par about pushing the yen  higher in case of Japanese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Views on the rupiah remained mixed, with some attributing\par the plunge to a one-off outflow of foreign money and others\par saying risks on the political and reform front and falling\par interest rates were now overshadowing the bullishness on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders said the trigger for the rupiah's sharp slide was\par the news earlier this week that BP Plc (BP.L) and global mining\par giant Rio Tinto (RIO.L) (RIO.AX) were selling their Indonesian\par coal mine joint venture to a local firm for $500 million.\par     "There's nothing in terms of fundamentals that has\par changed," said Ray Farris, strategist with Credit Suisse First\par Boston.\par     "All that has happened is that the single most crowded\par trade in the region has now been flattened out. Everyone was\par short the dollar/rupiah and they are all trying to get out\par through a very small door at the same time."\par  \par     Farris said the rupiah would probably recover to about\par 8,400 or higher by the end of the year.\par     While currently there were no takers for the rupiah other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the balance of payments was strong with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around two billion dollars worth of trade surplus every month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and potential capital inflows from government asset sales, he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FOCUS ON POLICY CHANGES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, Thailand's move on Wednesday to open its capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets was a talking point among traders.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shrewd central banks were coping with growing pressure to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate and cut down \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par encouraging foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  outflows through easing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regulations, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China and Taiwan are expected to relax rules on their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capital accounts soon, India introduced rupee options, and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines is contemplating reversing some rigid rules on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hedging.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand increased the amount that domestic investors could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold in foreign bonds and extended the period exporters could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold non-baht revenues in their foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accounts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is another example of how pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strengthen has resulted in welcome relaxations of trade and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment constraints," Deutsche Bank said in a note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The baht fell to a three-week low past 42 per dollar on the\par news, but was slightly stronger on Thursday morning.\par     "The Bank of Thailand knows that with an outperforming Thai\par economy, it cannot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indefinitely to prevent underlying\par U.S. dollar weakness against baht," DBS Bank said in a note.\par     Rising stocks supported the Korean won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the Singapore dollar  too firmed to a two-week high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closer to 1.75 as overseas players continued unwinding their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short Sing dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0300 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.84       118.82         -0.02\par  Sing dlr      1.7514       1.7562         +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.357       34.417         +0.17\par  Korean won   1180.20      1182.80         +0.22\par  Baht           41.96        41.99         +0.07\par  Peso           54.17        54.03         -0.25\par  Rupiah       8675.00      8550.00         -1.44\par     Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.84       118.74         -0.08\par  Sing dlr      1.7514       1.7341         -0.99\par  Taiwan dlr    34.357       34.753         +1.15\par  Korean won   1180.20      1185.80         +0.47\par  Baht           41.96        43.08         +2.67\par  Peso           54.17        53.38         -1.45\par  Rupiah       8675.00      8940.00         +3.05.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030724dz7o006sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
