\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Rupiah Looking Vulnerable \b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2003\par 12:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday to halt the slide in the rupiah, which is showing signs of fatigue after a 20-month bull run. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the region, the Philippine peso and Thai baht weakened, while the Singapore dollar, New Taiwan dollar and South Korea won ended stronger. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, Bank Indonesia Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has fallen nearly 4% from levels just two days ago. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a three-month high of IDR8,650 in morning trading before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the local unit recover slightly. Late in Asian trading the dollar was quoted at IDR8,610, up from IDR8,425 late Tuesday in Asia and IDR8,320 Monday. \par \par \uc2  At its peak in May, the rupiah had rallied more than 35% from a low of 11,000 to the dollar in November 2001. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have attributed the rupiah's recent decline to a number of factors, including Indonesia's plan to exit the International Monetary Fund program at the end of the year, the potential for increased political risk linked to next year's presidential elections, and the narrowing in Indonesia's interest-rate differential. \par \par \uc2  "While we once had the rupiah overshooting to 7,500 (per dollar) in the third quarter, we will be changing the numbers this week to around 9,000 by end-September," JP Morgan strategist James Malcolm said in a research report. \par \par \uc2  Over the past five years, IMF funding has widely been seen as a disciplinary mechanism for the Indonesian government to push through much-needed economic reforms, said Fauzi Ichsan, an economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  Last year, however, the parliament issued a decree requesting the government not to extend the program into 2004. \par \par \uc2  In Manila, the peso hit a four-month low against the dollar as businesses continued to accumulate dollars to be used for imports of goods for the Christmas shopping season. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at PHP54.025 on the Philippine dealing system, up from PHP53.850 late Tuesday. That was the dollar's strongest close against the peso since March 25, when it ended at PHP54.300. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the dollar gained ground after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would ease restrictions on investment in foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt, and raise the time limit on exporter dollar holdings to six months from three months. \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed as high as THB42.080 after the announcement, but relinquished some of those gains to trade around THB41.980 late in the session versus THB41.810 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The new rules should increase institutional demand for dollars and could decrease supply from exporters. The dollar demand will also help to prevent any excessive appreciation in the baht. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar, Singapore dollar and won benefited from spillover strength in the yen. Against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was quoted at Y118.72 in late Asian trading, compared with Y119.04 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar got an additional boost from continued foreign inflows to the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$34.417, down from  NT$34.441 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net NT$1.23 billion in Taiwan shares Wednesday, according to the Taiwan Stock Exchange. \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, dollar sales by local corporations added to the pressure on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar's fall was firmly supported around KRW1,180, however, as importers continued to buy dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at KRW1,180.9, down from KRW1,182.8 late Tuesday, after trading within a narrow range of KRW1,179.9-KRW1,182.8. \par \par \uc2  Improving prospects for Singapore's economic recovery helped fuel the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7562, down from S$1.7581 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Although the Singapore economy contracted by an estimated 4.3% in the second quarter from a year ago due largely to the SARS outbreak, economists widely expect a sharp rebound in the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  United Overseas Bank said the improved outlook should keep the trade-weighted Singapore dollar trading in the stronger half of the policy band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  guides the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2  1136 1159 1848 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030723dz7n000oa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
