\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing slips, won rises as policy eased. \b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2003\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 10 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar fell\par sharply on Thursday when the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly\par eased monetary policy and data showed a large contraction in\par the economy, but pared its losses in afternoon trade.\par     Equity-related inflows boosted the South Korean won\par   to a five-month closing high even after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut rates to record lows and said the economy, one of\par Asia's stars in recent years, was in recession for the first\par time since the 1997/98 Asian crisis.\par     Indonesia also cut interest rates on Thursday to join\par Thailand, the Philippines, Taiwan and Hong Kong in easing\par policy since the U.S Federal Reserve cut rates on June 25.\par     The Singapore dollar slumped to 1.7608 per dollar after the\par easing from 1.7480 just before the announcement. Later it\par recovered towards 1.7500 as foreign funds that had held long\par U.S. dollars positions booked some profits.\par     "The market is still digesting the policy move.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  It seems\par 1.76 will take some time to break, but the Sing dollar will be\par weaker," said a dealer at a local bank.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, which targets the\par trade-weighted exchange rate rather than interest rates, said\par it would re-centre its policy band around the current level of\par the Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate.\par     Analysts said as the Singapore dollar was about 1.4 to 2.0\par percent on the weaker side of the previous mid-point, the\par adjustment meant MAS would target a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The MAS is conducting a policy of gradual devaluation of\par the trade-weighted Sing dollar," said Adam Le Mesurier, an\par analyst at Goldman Sachs in Singapore. He said the MAS has now\par weakened its NEER target by five percent in the last 18 months.\par     Separate data showed the economy shrank an annualised 11.8\par percent in the second quarter, against a four percent fall that\par markets had forecast. The government has said it expects an\par economic upturn in the second half of the year.\par     "We believe there is not enough visibility on the global\par economic environment yet to shift away from our core view of\par being long Singapore bonds, and short the Sing dollar NEER," Le\par Mesurier said.\par     WON STAYS BID\par     The South Korean won                   posted its strongest\par close in five months at 1,178.4 per dollar, boosted by foreign\par fund inflows into local stocks despite a weaker market.\par     The won showed little reaction to the Bank of Korea cutting\par its call rate to a record low of 3.75 percent and downgrading\par its 2003 growth forecast to 3.1 percent from 4.1 percent.\par     The Taiwan dollar          ended marginally higher, after\par hitting a 10-month high of 34.25 per U.S. dollar, helped by\par equity-related inflows and a firmer yen .\par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , for the third time this week,\par pulled the Taiwan dollar off its highs before the local close.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        eased to the weaker side of\par 8,200 per dollar on what dealers in Jakarta said was\par profit-taking on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent gains.\par     Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut is benchmark rate by 75 basis\par points to 9.0 percent following a further decline on the\par benchmark SBI interest rate in its weekly auction. It was the\par sixth cut since May 1, when the rate stood at 11.25 percent.\par     The Thai baht        fluctuated in a 41.59-41.75 per dollar\par range, easing along with the Sing dollar early on and later\par rising as the Sing dollar stabilised.\par     The market showed little response to Bank of Thailand\par Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula comments that the baht would be\par left to move with market forces. Dealers have said the BOT\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervented\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the baht around 51.50 in June and early\par July. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0828 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.71       118.12         +0.35\par  Sing dlr      1.7524       1.7544         +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.246       34.337         +0.27\par  Korean won   1178.40      1179.00         +0.05\par  Baht           41.64        41.68         +0.10\par  Peso           53.41        53.43         +0.04\par  Rupiah       8213.00      8195.00         -0.22\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.71       118.74         +0.88\par  Sing dlr      1.7524       1.7341         -1.04\par  Taiwan dlr    34.246       34.753         +1.48\par  Korean won   1178.40      1185.80         +0.63\par  Baht           41.64        43.08         +3.46\par  Peso           53.41        53.38         -0.06\par  Rupiah       8213.00      8940.00         +8.85.\par 