\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Dn Late; \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves Rise Sparks Easing Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2003\par 10:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was weaker late Tuesday, after a reported surge in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fueled speculation of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing this week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0810 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7555, up from S$1.7498 late in Asia Monday. It traded between S$1.7540 and S$1.7570 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened around S$1.7570, keeping pace with its advances against counterparts such as the yen and the euro in overnight trade. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held on to its gains on speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have bought U.S. dollars ahead of a monetary policy easing this week, after data issued late Monday showed a sharp rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the second straight month. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, where the impact of trade swamps a small domestic economy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore conducts monetary policy via the exchange rate, rather than interest rates. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar when the economy needs a boost or push up the local unit when it wants to control inflation or an economic overheating. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose 1% on month to US$86.62 billion in June, according to MAS data. \par \par \uc2  "That this comes two days before the widely-watched MAS policy statement has only led to further speculation of possible change by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," United Overseas Bank said in a research report. \par \par \uc2  The MAS will issue its semiannual monetary policy review Thursday, but most market participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its currently neutral policy stance. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore government will also issue key second-quarter economic data on Thursday, which are widely expected to show a contraction in gross domestic product. Most analysts, however, expect growth to resume in subsequent quarters. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to stay between S$1.7500 and S$1.7580 in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds ended lower Tuesday as they tracked continued weakness in Japanese government bonds, and following the overnight fall in U.S. Treasurys, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local bonds have also been under pressure after recent signs emerged that the trade-reliant Singapore economy, although expected to contract in the second quarter, could rebound in subsequent quarters. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was up 5 basis points at 0.86%, while the yield on five-year bonds was up 7 basis points at 1.61%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was 6 basis points higher at 2.07%, while the yield on 10-year bonds rose 10 basis points to 2.51%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was 9 basis points higher at 2.81%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, offers were higher, tracking local\par bond yields. The two-year offer rose 2 basis points to 1.00%, while the\par five-year swap offer increased six basis points to 1.75%. The 10-year\par offer was up 7 basis points at 2.61%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 161 basis points\par from late Monday's 156 basis points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly flat or modestly higher,\par though liquidity remained flush in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Tuesday      Late Monday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.5000% 0.6250%   0.3750% 0.4375%\par 3-Month           0.4375% 0.5625%   0.4375% 0.5625%\par 1-Year            0.6250% 0.7500%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Bernice Tang & Ryan Woo\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030708dz78000in\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
