\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bow to U.S. dlr rally, c.bank worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2003\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, July 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped back\par from their recent highs early on Tuesday, happy to cede ground\par to a U.S. dollar that was strengthened by a U.S. equities\par rally.\par     Dealers said the dollar's rise and worries about\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian central banks had raised doubts about\par sustainability of gains in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including the\par yen , which was holding around 118 per dollar.\par     Asian stock markets, impressed by Wall Street's rally, were\par poised for more gains which would attract more foreign\par investment that should offer Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  some support.\par     Dealers said those investment inflows were likely to invite\par more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian central banks, several of whom had\par been spotted buying dollars in recent sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The South Korean won                   held on to a firm\par bias, aided by stock-related flows, but stayed clear of its\par five-month highs after Monday's heavy dollar buying by\par state-run banks, suspected to be acting on behalf of\par authorities.\par  \par     Dealers said about $1 billion was spent on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Taiwan dollar          was up, but wary of Monday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10-month highs after dealers spotted aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just before Monday's close of trade. Traders\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was active on Tuesday morning as well.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par James Malcolm, JP Morgan Chase's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist in\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said in a note that the Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 34.30 per U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Equity strength was the main reason for recent Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar appreciation," said Malcolm. Further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unlikely given the signal by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tends to be less comfortable with sharp\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, at least until global and regional data turns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decidedly positive," he wrote.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SGD CAUTION\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  eased to 1.7574 per U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from late Monday's 1.7498. It had weakened to 1.7588\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar in offshore trade, its lowest in four sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Players were cautious on the Sing dollar ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's monetary policy review. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore manages the dollar, its main policy tool, against a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of major trade partners and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said thin trading volumes ahead of the review could\par make price action in the Singapore dollar volatile.\par     The Thai baht        eased to around 41.64 per dollar,\par against Monday's one-week high of 41.52, with some offshore\par banks spotted buying dollars.\par     Dealers said the moves in major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and fear of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities to cap baht's strength had prompted\par players to cut back on short U.S. dollar positions.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        also came under selling\par pressure easing back close to the 8,200 per dollar level, after\par a hitting a one-month high of 8,153 on Monday.\par     The Philippine peso        respected its month-long range,\par and was slightly easier at around 53.39 per dollar after\par closing Monday's local trade at 53.35.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0212 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.17       117.99         -0.15\par  Sing dlr      1.7556       1.7498         -0.33\par  Taiwan dlr    34.365       34.405         +0.12\par  Korean won   1179.50      1181.90         +0.20\par  Baht           41.67        41.59         -0.19\par  Peso           53.39        53.35         -0.07\par  Rupiah       8190.00      8167.00         -0.28\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \