\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firm,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  trims some gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2003\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 7 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mostly\par stronger on Monday, but some saw their gains reversed by\par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even after European finance ministers\par had voiced concern over Asia's tight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management.\par     The Chinese yuan            was also in focus after the\par communique from the weekend meeting of the European and Asian\par finance ministers (ASEM) meeting in Bali mentioned a need for a\par "fairly shared adjustment of international imbalances."\par     The Taiwan dollar          retreated from a 10-month high,\par and dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had aggressively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par after five days of gains. The South Korean won\par was knocked off a five-month high by heavy dollar buying by\par state-run banks.\par     Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fared better. The Indonesian\par rupiah  rose to one-month high, and the Singapore dollar\par   and Thai baht        saw their strongest in over a week.\par The Philippine peso  ended local trade slightly higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Today's moves in Asia regionals and even dollar/yen\par suggest that the comments at Bali were not totally ignored,"\par said David Simmonds, strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland.\par     In closed-door meetings, European ministers pressured Asian\par governments to let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise against the dollar,\par and stop Europe from bearing the economic brunt of a weaker\par dollar.\par     The International Monetary Fund also urged China adopt\par greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility. While China manages the\par yuan in a 8.2760/8.2800 per dollar band, many Asian countries,\par including Japan, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak.\par     The discount on one-year yuan non-deliverable forwards to\par buy U.S. dollars  rose to 1,525 points on Monday, from\par Friday's 1,350 pips. It later pulled back to around 1,450 pips.\par     Last month it hit a record of 1,900 points.\par     Analysts said while traders would want to keep the\par revaluation trade alive, authorities in Beijing are more likely\par to live up to their repeated denial of any imminent move.\par     "We have to keep expectations at a realistic level,"\par Simmonds said, adding neither Japan not China, countries that\par make up the largest chunk of Asia's trade surplus, were likely\par to make any dramatic changes to their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy stance\par soon.\par     Late on Monday, Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said\par foreign authorities would likely tolerate "smoothing"\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the yen by Japan, and added he did not expect\par China to change its yuan policy soon as it would lead to\par unsteady growth.\par     POLICY REVIEW\par     Trade in the Singapore dollar was the most volatile of the\par regionals as the market speculated over the contents of\par Thursday's semi-annual monetary policy review.\par     A poll by Reuters last week had most analysts looking for\par no change in the neutral policy stance of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, which uses the exchange rate as its\par main policy tool.\par     The Singapore dollar touched 1.7476 per U.S. dollar, its\par strongest since June 26, before falling back to the 1.7500\par level.\par     In Taiwan, a government decision to abolish a ceiling on\par foreign investment in the the local stock market added to the\par regional momentum and pushed the TAIEX index  to a near\par one-year high, supporting the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0844 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.99       118.09         +0.08\par  Sing dlr      1.7498       1.7510         +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.405       34.390         -0.04\par  Korean won   1181.90      1180.20         -0.14\par  Baht           41.59        41.62         +0.07\par  Peso           53.35        53.40         +0.09\par  Rupiah       8167.00      8178.00         +0.13\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.99       118.74         +0.64\par  Sing dlr      1.7498       1.7341         -0.90\par  Taiwan dlr    34.405       34.753         +1.01\par  Korean won   1181.90      1185.80         +0.33\par  Baht           41.59        43.08         +3.58\par  Peso           53.35        53.38         +0.06\par  Rupiah       8167.00      8940.00         +9.46.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030707dz7700jlm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
