\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing slips, others hold small gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2003\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 20 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar slipped\par to a one-week low on Friday afternoon, wiping out its early\par gains even as other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found some support from\par the U.S. dollar's soft tone against the yen .\par  \par     The Singapore dollar weakened as far as 1.7361 per U.S.\par dollar, after opening local trade just shy of 1.7300.\par     Dealers said persistent Sing dollar offers from some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  foreign banks around 1.7300-1.7320 prompted a trimming of long \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar positions they were reluctant to hold over the \par \par \uc2  weekend. \par \par \uc2  That reluctance stemed from uncertainty over the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar, which could become more volatile as markets debate the \par \par \uc2  size of an expected rate cut by the U.S. Federal Reserve next \par \par \uc2  week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore releases its policy \par \par \uc2  review in early July, which should provide some medium term \par \par \uc2  direction for the Singapore dollar, its main policy tool. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed meeting has become a focal point here as most \par \par \uc2  people think their decision would have a strong influence on \par \par \uc2  Singapore's policy," said a senior dealer at a local bank in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, players were cautious of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains after \par \par \uc2  profit-taking in the region's stock markets trimmed some of \par \par \uc2  their recent gains, although foreign portfolio investors \par \par \uc2  continued to be net buyers in most Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  "Asian economies will do well even if the recovery in the \par \par \uc2  U.S. is a sluggish one and that is what most fund managers are \par \par \uc2  positioning for," said Philip Wee, strategist at DBS Bank. \par \par \uc2  Those portfolio inflows have put pressure on Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate, a proposition unacceptable to central \par \par \uc2  banks in the region given their sensitivity to export \par \par \uc2  competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  BAHT CONTAINED \par \par \uc2  Authorities in Thailand are among those dealers said had \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily this week, to counter the impact of foreign \par \par \uc2  portfolio inflows which have topped 18 billion baht this year. \par \par \uc2  The baht held a 41.56-41.60 per dollar range, holding above \par \par \uc2  Thursday's one-week low of 41.64, its upside capped by worries \par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the stock market edging off three-year \par \par \uc2  highs. \par \par \uc2  "The baht at the moment is quite stable which is good for \par \par \uc2  the real sector," Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn \par \par \uc2  Devakula told reporters on Friday. "And we are monitoring the \par \par \uc2  baht to ensure competitiveness." \par \par \uc2  Worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the South \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean won's             rise on Friday even though\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investors purchased a net 114 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won touched an intraday high of 1,187.0 per dollar, off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a Thursday's two-week low, but later pulled back to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,194.0.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     It stayed clear of Thursday's four-month high of 1,181.6\par which had prompted some aggressive Bank of Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     A dealer in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Korean state banks had bought\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about $400 million on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surpassing the $325 million worth of stock purchases made by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investors on the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign equity investors have been net buyers of Korean\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shares for 17 consecutive sessions, and have bought a net 1.11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trillion won in shares so far this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  rose to a near two-week high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 53.23 per dollar, supported by Thursday's report of a lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than expected budget deficit for the five months to March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dollar bids by corporates and importers trimmed those\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains, pulling it down to 53.30 by close of local trade,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers in Manila said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0825 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.32       118.60         +0.24\par  Sing dlr      1.7354       1.7317         -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.587       34.614         +0.08\par  Korean won   1190.50      1198.50         +0.67\par  Baht           41.58        41.60         +0.05\par  Peso           53.30        53.