\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won rises, but others lack drive. \b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2003\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 19 (Reuters) - The South Korean won pushed\par to a four-month high on Thursday, but other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par were easier against a U.S. dollar finding support as markets\par scaled back their expectations of an aggressive U.S. rate cut\par next week.\par     Dealers said the impact of an easier yen        on regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be countered to an extent by foreign equity\par investment flows.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar        was off the lows it hit in\par offshore trade, but was still down from late on Wednesday.\par     The Taiwan dollar was off Wednesday's five-month highs and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  the worry of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped keep the Thai \par \par \uc2  baht  away from its near 11-month high of 41.40 per \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah eased to its lowest in about a week, \par \par \uc2  and the Philippine peso  held close to 53.40 per dollar \par \par \uc2  ahead of budget deficit data due later in the day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won             rose to 1,182.0 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, its strongest level since February, as foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors continued to buy local shares. Net purchases by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreigners have topped two trillion won over the past couple of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, caution against possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were seen capping gains. Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said they\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par believed some Korean banks in recent sessions had been buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollars on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the dollar/yen move and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sensitivity to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength were restraining \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par across the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the market was still likely to favour holding short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar positions, given the support the regionals are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drawing from equity-related capital flows, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I'll still be positioning for short dollars across Asia,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I wouldn't be looking for a lot of downside (for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar) in the near term. It's more of a trade to sit on for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while as directionally this seems to be better than the other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par direction."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bhanu Baweja, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS in Singapore,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said in a note that the four-week moving average of net foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows into Asian equity markets had risen to $1 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He warned that the pressure from these flows on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to appreciate would be opposed by the region's central banks.\par     "Expect greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Asian central banks as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par these inflows put pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beyond what the current account surpluses are already\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exerting," he said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0245 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.61       118.33         -0.24\par  Sing dlr      1.7321       1.7285         -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.584       34.545         -0.11\par  Korean won   1183.80      1184.90         +0.09\par  Baht           41.61        41.54         -0.17\par  Peso           53.39        53.39          0.00\par  Rupiah       8243.00      8215.00         -0.34\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.61       118.74         +0.11\par  Sing dlr      1.7321       1.7341         +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr    34.584       34.753         +0.49\par  Korean won   1183.80      1185.80         +0.17\par  Baht           41.61        43.08         +3.53\par  Peso           53.39        53.38         -0.02\par  Rupiah       8243.00      8940.00         +8.46.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030619dz6j0066d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
