\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -China reins in speculation, won firms. \b0\par\par\uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2003\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 17 (Reuters) - The Korean won rose to a 3-=\par   month high alongside a surging Korean stock market and China\par curtailed some of the intense speculation in yuan forwards by\par reiterating its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy had not changed.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were rangebound on Tuesday, watching\par a listless U.S. dollar which was waiting on U.S. consumer price\par data for clues as to whether the Fed would cut rates next week.\par     And, as in Japan where fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped the\par yen, traders suspected regional central banks were the reason\par for the limited moves in the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Singapore dollar        made light gains during the day\par but was shy of 1.7250, from where it bounced lower last month,\par and traders remained apprehensive about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "They (the MAS) are keeping it fairly close-ranged, within\par a one to two percent band," James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par at JP Morgan said, referring to the undisclosed trade-weighted\par band authorities manage the Sing dollar in.\par  \par     Malcolm advised positioning for an appreciation in the\par Singapore dollar, but over three to six months.\par     He said even the Thai authorities seemed to have been\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein in the baht, although less aggressively\par than in the past.\par     The Thai baht        clung to 41.50, after it had equalled\par a near 11-month high of 41.40 in offshore deals. The Philippine\par peso's  spike higher past 53.40 was fleeting.\par     Malcolm said it was too far-fetched for markets to position\par for firmer Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the basis of the ongoing\par speculation in the yuan , or renminbi, forwards.\par     Forward premiums on the one-year yuan           hit a\par record 1,900 points but then fell back after China said there\par was no change to its policy of keeping the yuan stable.\par     Premiums have been rising since last week and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculative trade gathered steam early on Tuesday after U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Treasury Secretary John Snow said the United States would back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any plan by China to move toward a more flexible exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malcolm said some banks had suggested a yuan revaluation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would boost other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because it would reduce the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worries about export competitiveness against China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "That's a very long-term thing, not one to position for\par immediately," he said.\par     RUPIAH STALLS, WON GAINS\par     The Taiwan dollar          rose in line with the Korean won\par              as Korean stocks         hit six-month highs.\par     The won's gains were also reflected in the yen-won cross\par rate . The cross rate moved to 10.05 from Monday's\par 10.16, showing the won was gaining ground against the yen.\par     The rupiah, Asia's strongest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year, could not progress much beyond 8,185. The rupiah has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par encountered resistance and bounced several times in recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weeks off a rising trendline drawn through the its 33-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high of 8,085 on May 26 and its June 10 high of 8,150.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said heavy foreign investment inflows, the latest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par being the approximate $365 million received by Indonesia's Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Restructuring Agency for a 51 percent stake sale in Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Danamon (BDMN.JK), had also waned.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And analysts said despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Indonesia's (BI)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par apparent approval of a firmer \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the competitiveness of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against others in the region still mattered.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Thus, the rupiah should stay firm, but resistance is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to be found at 8,000, as long as the Bank of Japan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resists yen appreciation beyond 115, keeping other Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par central banks on the defensive," DBS Bank said in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commentary.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0842 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.63       117.51         -0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7262       1.7287         +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.522       34.599         +0.22\par  Korean won   1183.00      1190.10         +0.60\par  Baht           41.49        41.54         +0.12\par  Peso           53.41        53.40         -0.02\par  Rupiah       8195.00      8195.00          0.00\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.63       118.74         +0.94\par  Sing dlr      1.7262       1.7341         +0.46\par  Taiwan dlr    34.522       34.753         +0.67\par  Korean won   1183.00      1185.80         +0.24\par  Baht           41.49        43.08         +3.83\par  Peso           53.41        53.38         -0.06\par  Rupiah       8195.00      8940.00         +9.09.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030617dz6h00gu0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
