\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dollar sits tight amid China talk, policy worry. \b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2003\par 03:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     0050 GMT - Singapore dollar        sticks to a steady,\par tight range, unmoved by the U.S. dollar's swings, and is wary\par of moving near a psychological resistance at 1.7250\par  \par  - Traders said intensifying speculation China will allow a\par wider trading band for the yuan  and let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par appreciate was positive for Asia.\par  \par  - Yet, amid talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem gains in the\par Korean won, Taiwan dollar and Japanese yen by their respective\par central banks, traders are wary of buying these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par  - Meanwhile the U.S. dollar steadies off overnight highs\par as markets wait for key U.S. inflation data to provide a clue\par about whether the Fed will cut rates next week.\par  \par  - The Sing dollar  keeps to a 1.7270/80 range.\par  \par  - Markets still uncertain if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in May, when the Sing dollar rose to\par 1.7250.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  - But it fell very rapidly from that high to 1.74 and\par traders said that experience, which caused a lot of stop-loss\par offloading of positions, has made markets cautious.\par  \par  - The Thai baht  came off 41.40 in offshore deals\par and is seen meeting resistance at 41.50. It is quoted at\par 41.51/53.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030617dz6h0025y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
