\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Renewed momentum on U.S. dlr woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2003\par 06:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 16 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found fresh\par upward momentum on Monday morning after the U.S. dollar\par weakened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following weak consumer data\par which stoked expectations of a U.S. rate cut later this month.\par     The Singapore dollar        rose over a cent from Friday's\par lows, the Indonesian rupiah  was back on an uptrend that\par stalled in late May and heading towards the 33-month highs\par struck then, the Korean won             tested three-week\par highs and the Thai baht  rose to a 10-day peak.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are still rangebound, but within that the\par drift is for the U.S. dollar to trade lower," said Thio Chin\par Loo, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with BNP Paribas.\par     Also, asset markets were driving \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and with\par investments flowing into eurobonds, the foreign fund inflows\par would boost regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , she said.\par  \par     Some of the resistance to the Singapore dollar's\par appreciation also seemed to have waned, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Last week, the Sing had been undermined by expectations of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment outflows after a consortium led by Singapore's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Temasek Holdings and Germany's Deutsche Bank (DBKGn.DE) won the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bid for a majority stake in Indonesia's Bank Danamon (BDMN.JK).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week's widely-held view that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by buying dollars, after a $2.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion monthly rise in reserves in May, was also giving way to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scepticism, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculation next month's policy review would see the MAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par widen the undisclosed trade-weighted band the Sing dollar is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par allowed to move in, effectively easing policy, had also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moderated, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Singapore has passed the worst of the SARS outbreak," Thio\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said, referring to the Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par epidemic that has hit travel and spending in Asia since March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the MAS did not widen policy then, at the peak of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par epidemic, there is no reason to believe they will do so now,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  opened firmer after a long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend that included a holiday on Friday, boosted by bunched\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar inflows and the regional trend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  touched a four-week high as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock markets in Korea and Taiwan extended last week's gains.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0404 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.65       117.60         -0.04\par  Sing dlr      1.7270       1.7325         +0.32\par  Taiwan dlr    34.606       34.645         +0.11\par  Korean won   1190.60      1191.90         +0.11\par  Baht           41.55        41.59         +0.10\par  Peso           53.45        53.61         +0.30\par  Rupiah       8190.00      8215.00         +0.31\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.65       118.74         +0.93\par  Sing dlr      1.7270       1.7341         +0.41\par  Taiwan dlr    34.606       34.753         +0.42\par  Korean won   1190.60      1185.80         -0.40\par  Baht           41.55        43.08         +3.68\par  Peso           53.45        53.38         -0.13\par  Rupiah       8190.00      8940.00         +9.16.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030616dz6g008sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
