\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Flat, musing on policy. \b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2003\par 04:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 13 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mostly\par flat on Friday against a backdrop of rising regional stock\par markets, a steady yen and U.S. dollar, and wariness over policy\par moves to curtail gains and protect export competitiveness.\par     The worries over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and possible investment\par outflows hemmed in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar  and dampened\par moves in others such as the Thai baht  and Indonesian\par rupiah .\par     Traders in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the market was still worried\par about dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a $2.4 billion monthly rise in reserves in May.\par Next month's semi-annual monetary policy review also added to\par the market anxiety.\par      More immediate was the concern that there will be demand\par for U.S. dollars as a consortium led by Singapore's Temasek\par Holdings and Germany's Deutsche Bank (DBKGn.DE) makes the final\par payment for a majority stake in Indonesia's Bank Danamon\par  (BDMN.JK).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The consortium has already paid $15 million and Indonesia's\par Bank Restructuring Agency said the rest of the total estimated\par $363 million payment would be made by Friday. The cash payment\par would be split evenly between rupiah and dollars.\par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with JP Morgan, said he\par did not expect an impact on the Singapore dollar from the\par payment. It was anticipated and the MAS would likely ensure the\par market did not feel the pressure, he said.\par     Yet, the worries over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seemed justified.\par     "We know that the MAS are very concerned about the local\par and global economic picture and outlook. Anecdotally, they\par continue to be very active in the market in terms of keeping\par Sing dollar at a weak level,"Malcolm said.\par     "Even when you strip out the euro valuation effects and so\par on, they must have bought well over a billion (U.S.) dollars in\par the market in May to keep the Sing dollar weak," he said.\par     The Sing dollar was being kept about one to two percent on\par the weaker side of the mid-point of the undisclosed\par trade-weighted band that authorities manage it in, he said.\par     Yet, the chances that the MAS would widen this band to ease\par monetary policy at its July review were significantly less than\par 50 percent, he said.\par     WON INDIFFERENT\par     The Korean won                   was steady, shrugging off\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments on Thursday that exports were expected to\par strengthen in the second half of the year and spur the economy.\par     It was also indifferent to possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a\par finance ministry official said on Thursday authorities would\par counter the won's strength if necessary, saying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains\par were undesirable given slowing exports and economic activity.\par     "It's partly a reflection of the weak U.S. dollar\par continuing," said Greg Gibbs, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the\par Royal Bank of Canada Capital Markets.\par     That weak dollar trend could keep the won firm over the\par next month or so, although the policy intentions implied the\par authorities would fight the appreciation of the won, Gibbs\par said.\par     "The authorities there will resist that for sure," he said.\par     Markets in Philippines were closed on Friday. The peso\par   hit a 10-week low of 53.65 on Thursday after rating\par agency Fitch downgraded its sovereign foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was listless, as it has been\par for over a week, after a steep rally from mid-March to late\par May. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut overnight rates by half a percentage\par point on Thursday, the fifth cut since May.\par  \par     But analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained attractive for its\par high yield.\par     "It is attractive for yield play. It has just had such a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong run," Gibbs said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0150 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.71       117.63         -0.07\par  Sing dlr      1.7387       1.7374         -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.664       34.667         +0.01\par  Korean won   1192.70      1193.20         +0.04\par  Baht           41.70        41.70         +0.01\par  Rupiah       8245.00      8250.00         +0.06\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.71       118.74         +0.88\par  Sing dlr      1.7387       1.734