\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dollar pares losses, leads others. \b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2003\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 13 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar\par pared some of the week's losses late on Friday as traders\par squared some of their short positions ahead of the weekend,\par although uncertainty over policy and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  persisted.\par     The Sing's gains of half a cent from its early lows near\par 1.7390 per U.S dollar boosted others in the region such as the\par Thai baht  and Indonesian rupiah       .\par     The Singapore dollar has been under pressure all week as\par traders worried whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by buying dollars after a $2.4 billion monthly\par rise in reserves in May. Next month's semi-annual monetary\par policy review by the MAS also added to traders' anxiety.\par     The market had mixed views on the issue.\par     "In the run-up to the policy review, dollar-Singapore\par should stay fairly supported, although it depends on how high\par dollar-yen can go," said Jimmy Koh, head of research at United\par Overseas Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan, believed\par the MAS had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in May to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar,\par although he gave a less than 50 percent chance of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's trade-weighted band being widened at the July policy\par review.\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS, said the\par Singapore dollar appreciated by nearly one percent in nominal\par effective exchange rate terms in May. This did not support the\par view the MAS had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and he said\par the rise in reserves could have been on account of government\par asset sales.\par     "Though the growth outlook has worsened, I do not expect a\par change in policy because I have not found clear evidence that\par nominal changes in the exchange rate have a strong impact on\par trade pattern," he said in a note.\par     Separately, concerns waned of a spike in demand for U.S.\par dollars to fund the payment for a majority stake in Indonesia's\par Bank Danamon (BDMN.JK) from a consortium led by Singapore's\par Temasek Holdings and Germany's Deutsche Bank (DBKGn.DE).\par     The consortium has already paid $15 million and Indonesia's\par Bank Restructuring Agency said the rest of the total estimated\par $363 million payment would be made by Friday. The cash payment\par would be split evenly between rupiah and dollars.\par     WON INDIFFERENT\par     The Korean won                   rose slightly, shrugging\par off \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments on Thursday that exports were\par expected to strengthen in the second half of the year and spur\par the economy.\par     It was also indifferent to possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a\par finance ministry official said on Thursday authorities would\par counter the won's strength if necessary, saying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains\par were undesirable given slowing exports and economic activity.\par     Markets in Philippines were closed on Friday. The peso\par   hit a 10-week low of 53.65 on Thursday after rating\par agency Fitch downgraded its sovereign foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        rose in line with the Sing\par dollar, but stayed clear of recent highs around 8,150. The\par rupiah has stalled after a steep rally from mid-March to late\par May.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut overnight rates by half a percentage\par point on Thursday, the fifth cut since May, but analysts said\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained attractive for its high yield. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0845 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.60       117.63         +0.03\par  Sing dlr      1.7325       1.7374         +0.28\par  Taiwan dlr    34.645       34.667         +0.06\par  Korean won   1191.90      1193.20         +0.11\par  Baht           41.59        41.70         +0.26\par  Rupiah       8215.00      8250.00         +0.43\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.60       118.74         +0.97\par  Sing dlr      1.7325       1.7341         +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    34.645       34.753         +0.31\par  Korean won   1191.90      1185.80         -0.51\par  Baht           41.59        43.08         +3.58\par  Rupiah       8215.00      8940.00         +8.83.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030613dz6d00iit\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
