\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht gains, others tread water. \b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2003\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 12 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held tight\par ranges on Thursday as traders mulled mixed signals from rising\par equities, more grim economic data from Korea, and the threat of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the regional markets.\par     The U.S. dollar's fall to its low for the week against the\par euro  amid expectations of rate cuts in both the United\par States and euro zone had little influence on the local markets.\par     The Thai baht        was the strongest in the region,\par supported by its rising stock market and the foreign investment\par inflows. In contrast, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar  was weighed\par down by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders said the huge $2.4 billion monthly rise in reserves\par in May, reported last weekend, has been interpreted as a sure\par sign of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and has weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar this week.\par     Some analysts were sceptical of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talk.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "While we would never rule out the possibility of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the likelihood is that the generally soft\par economic outlook is becoming more manifest in the Singapore\par dollar, if not in other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," National Australia\par Bank said in a commentary.\par     "The other factor suggesting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has not taken\par place being the fact that the Sing dollar NEER (nominal\par effective exchange rate) remains mid-range," it said, referring\par to the undisclosed trade-weighted band the MAS manages the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in.\par     The Korean won                   strengthened after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Korea kept rates steady, as expected, despite a\par rise in unemployment to a 17-month high.\par  \par     The Bank of Korea said it expected stronger growth in the\par second half of the year, supported by strong exports.\par     Traders said that could mean they would also try to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won competitive in trade-weighted terms. That view was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supported when a finance ministry official said authorities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would counter the won's strength if necessary, saying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains were undesirable given slowing exports and economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par activity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Korea was not alone in its woes, and National Australia\par Bank said the regional economic outlook was not bullish.\par     "One reason we have been bearish Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is due to\par the struggling local economies," the National Australia Bank\par report said.\par     The Philippine peso        softened after rating agency\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fitch downgraded its sovereign foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating to BB\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from BB+, citing the weak fiscal position. Late on Thursday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government said the May budget deficit was 13.4 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pesos against a target of 20.5 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manila-based traders said the peso's decline stalled around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 53.65, a technical resistance for the dollar and an end-March\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low, and it then retraced some losses ahead of a holiday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend. Markets there are closed on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  extended its decline as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players booked profits after a long rally. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest rates for the fifth time\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since the start of May, bringing the overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate to 9.75 percent - still the highest in Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia also said it had signed a deal on economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reforms with the International Monetary Fund, which would pave\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the way for the release of the next tranche of an IMF loan of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about $450 million by early next month.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0850 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.63       117.80         +0.14\par  Sing dlr      1.7374       1.7362         -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.667       34.682         +0.04\par  Korean won   1193.20      1195.20         +0.17\par  Baht           41.70        41.82         +0.30\par  Peso           53.61        53.54         -0.13\par  Rupiah       8250.00      8226.00         -0.29\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.63       118.74         +0.94\par  Sing dlr      1.7374       1.7341         -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.667       34.753         +0.25\par  Korean won   1193.20      1185.80         -0.62\par  Baht           41.70        43.08         +3.32\par  Peso           53.61        53.38         -0.43\par  Rupiah       8250.00      8940.00         +8.36.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030612dz6c00jb9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
