\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dollar at month low, peso slips. \b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2003\par 05:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, June 12 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mostly\par weaker on Thursday morning and quite indifferent to the fall in\par the U.S. dollar as markets worried that gains might provoke\par policy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect export competitiveness.\par     The Korean won            went against the trend, finding\par support from a rising stock market despite unemployment\par reaching a 17-month high. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left official\par interest rates steady after its meeting on Thursday.\par     The Philippine peso        softened after rating agency\par Fitch downgraded its sovereign foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating to BB\par from BB+, citing the weak fiscal position.\par     The Singapore dollar        led its neighbours as it\par dropped to a one-month low near 1.74 per dollar, although the\par Thai baht  was almost unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said data on Singapore's foreign reserves for May,\par released on the weekend, continued to be a drag on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par after markets interpreted the huge $2.4 billion monthly rise in\par reserves as a sure sign of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The wariness about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength will continue for two\par main reasons," said David Simmonds, strategist with the Royal\par Bank of Scotland in Singapore.\par     "Although there are still hopes of a U.S.-led growth in the\par second half of the year, lead indicators for Asian exports\par still don't look particularly strong and therefore policymakers\par are going to remain wary, especially as we enter the season of\par the most heavily SARS-affected data over the next quarter or\par two."\par     Moreover, the soft U.S. dollar meant Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par also losing competitiveness against the nearly pegged Chinese\par yuan, he said.\par  \par     "Less competitiveness against China is profoundly what\par policymakers don't want at this stage," Simmonds said.\par     RUPIAH PAUSES\par     The Indonesian rupiah        extended its decline as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players booked profits after a long rally. Meanwhile\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest rates for the fifth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par time the start of May, bringing the overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 9.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia also said it had signed a letter of economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reforms with the International Monetary Fund, which would pave\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the way for the release of the next tranche of an IMF loan of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about $450 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Manila, traders were not too perturbed about the rating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par change or the slight decline in the peso to 53.65, a low seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in late March. Markets will be closed on Friday for a holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Ahead of the weekend and likely bunched overseas worker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows, no one's going to be going too long dollars," a trader\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Besides, a part of the dollar buying in recent weeks had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been to fund investments in the sovereign eurobond issues as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par onshore players too joined the search for high-yielding assets,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0301 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.91       117.80         -0.09\par  Sing dlr      1.7380       1.7362         -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.684       34.682         -0.01\par  Korean won   1193.90      1195.20         +0.11\par  Baht           41.81        41.82         +0.02\par  Peso           53.59        53.54         -0.09\par  Rupiah       8257.00      8226.00         -0.38\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.91       118.74         +0.70\par  Sing dlr      1.7380       1.7341         -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr    34.684       34.753         +0.20\par  Korean won   1193.90      1185.80         -0.68\par  Baht           41.81        43.08         +3.04\par  Peso           53.59        53.38         -0.39\par  Rupiah       8257.00      8940.00         +8.27.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030612dz6c006mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
