\par\par \b \uc2  Sing dollar, baht slip,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worries weigh. \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2003\par 03:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     0050 GMT -- The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        loses ground\par against the U.S. dollar, indifferent to the latter's losses\par against the euro, as worries over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  affect sentiment.\par  \par  - Traders expect a similar reluctance to rally and benefit\par from the U.S. dollar's woes in most of the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par matching the Japanese yen .\par  \par  - The Sing dollar drops to near 1.74 in opening deals,\par nearly half a cent from levels late on Wednesday. The baht\par slips too, to 41.81/85 per dollar\par  \par  - Rising equity markets and foreign equity inflows into\par Asia and the U.S. dollar's weakness based on interest\par differentials and economic data should exert upward pressure on\par the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par  \par  - But traders suspect central banks have been thwarting\par gains in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par  - Data showing Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves grew\par by US$2.4 billion to US$85.8 billion in May suggested the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in May, traders\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Reporting by