\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bracing for gains from equity flows. \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, June 11 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were steady\par to slightly weaker against a range-bound U.S. dollar on\par Wednesday as regional equity markets rose and traders braced\par for further climbs in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Singapore dollar        was slightly weaker around\par 1.7350, the Thai baht  kept to a narrower band around\par 41.80 while the Indonesian rupiah  was dragged back to\par the weaker side of 8,200. Traders said the market had merely\par paused to book profits on long positions in these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Korean won                   began the day firm, buoyed\par by rising stock markets and foreign investor inflows, but later\par buckled under suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Equity markets are still holding well and that places some\par upside pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Thio Chin Loo, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with BNP Paribas, Singapore.\par     Still, with the dollar and the euro        hemmed in by\par rate cut uncertainties, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade would be muted,\par she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of America said in its daily commentary Asian stock\par markets had received over $1.3 billion of foreign equity\par investments so far during the month, with a big chunk going to\par Korea and Taiwan.\par  \par     And on Wednesday, stock markets in Japan, Australia, Korea\par and Taiwan hit multi-month highs.\par     "We remain convinced that export competitiveness is seen as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a critical goal by most central banks in the region, especially\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in an environment of slowing global income," Bank of America\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said in the note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We expect most central banks to maintain a policy towards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted weakness, and this would also entail absorbing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any large capital inflow to prevent a sharp appreciation."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     On Wednesday, as the baht slipped, the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par denied \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the previous day to slow the baht's gains.\par     BNP Paribas's Thio however said in a note she suspected the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in May.\par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves grew by US$2.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion to US$85.8 billion in May, suggesting that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was fairly aggressive as trade flows were unlikely to have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improved in that month, although this is pure conjecture at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this stage with trade data not released yet," the note said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0815 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.80       118.15         +0.30\par  Sing dlr      1.7362       1.7318         -0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.682       34.675         -0.02\par  Korean won   1195.20      1194.20         -0.08\par  Baht           41.82        41.75         -0.17\par  Peso           53.54        53.37         -0.32\par  Rupiah       8226.00      8195.00         -0.38\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.80       118.74         +0.80\par  Sing dlr      1.7362       1.7341         -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr    34.682       34.753         +0.20\par  Korean won   1195.20      1185.80         -0.79\par  Baht           41.82        43.08         +3.01\par  Peso           53.54        53.38         -0.29\par  Rupiah       8226.00      8940.00         +8.68.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030611dz6b00ioc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
