\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Late; Market Wary Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 11:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the yen lower Wednesday, with market players remaining wary of provoking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional central banks. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won initially proved the exception as equity related dollar selling by foreign investors pushed the U.S. unit to an intraday trough of KRW1,190.7. Foreign investors snapped up local shares for a 10th session, ending as net buyers of KRW155.9 billion of stocks. \par \par \uc2  But the Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar, buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the KRW1,191 level, pushing it all the way to an intraday high of KRW1,196.4, a foreign bank trader in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at KRW1,195.4, modestly higher from KRW1,194.5 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  State-run banks bought as much as $700 million-$800 million, likely on behalf of the authorities, a Seoul-based trader said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign equity inflows have been a key factor underpinning the strength of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. Bank of America said Asian stock markets, led by Taiwan and Korea, have seen equity investments of over $1.3 billion to date in June. \par \par \uc2  However, "we remain convinced that export competitiveness is seen as a critical goal by most central banks in the region, especially in an environment of slowing global income," the bank said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  "We expect most central banks to maintain a policy toward trade-weighted weakness, and this would also entail absorbing any large capital inflow to prevent a sharp appreciation," Bank of America added. \par \par \uc2  Continued U.S. dollar buying related to military equipment purchases, and also the yen's weakness, weighed on the New Taiwan dollar, although this was partly offset by foreign inflows to the stock market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit ended at NT$34.682, up from NT$34.677 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought more than NT$4 billion worth of shares Wednesday, although the main index fell 0.6% to snap a four-session winning streak. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar fell to a one-week low as market players exercised caution on talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days to keep the local unit weak to aid the city-state's flagging economy. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data, issued over the weekend, appear to lend support to the speculation. \par \par \uc2  "Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grew by $2.4 billion to $85.8 billion in May, suggesting that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fairly aggressive as trade flows were unlikely to have improved in that month, although this is pure conjecture at this stage with trade data not released yet," BNP Paribas said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the ascent of the SGD (\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar) falls into the current monetary policy stance of the Authority, where a guarded growth outlook justifies an accommodative monetary policy stance," the French bank added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears also kept the Thai baht on a weaker footing, although this was offset by equity related dollar selling by offshore institutional players, a trader in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the dollar was quoted around 41.81 baht, marginally up from THB41.79 Tuesday. The trader said the dollar selling took hold when it reached the "high 80s." \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso closed lower as banks bought dollars in anticipation of a possible downgrade of the country's credit rating, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 53.535 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP53.365 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A Manila newspaper reported Wednesday that Fitch Ratings will downgrade its long-term credit rating on the Philippines to "BB" from "BB+" due to the government's growing debt burden, fiscal deficit, and election-related concerns that raise doubts on the continuity of economic policies. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the market can't actively push the dollar higher as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to be selling dollars at PHP53.55. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco called the peso's weakness a "knee-jerk reaction" to reports of the possible downgrade and not an adverse view of the macroeconomic fundamentals which remain "sound." \par \par \uc2  "There has been an improvement on the revenue collection, (economic) growth is consistent, and inflation is low," Tetangco said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was marginally lower as market players took profit amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is trading at more than two-year highs after a 10% rally since the start of the year, as overseas investors put money into high-yielding stocks and bonds. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week said any further slide in the dollar would hurt exporters, and this has resulted in traders turning more cautious and taking profit on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed the local session at 8,230 rupiah, up from IDR8,210 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030611dz6b000lu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
