\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down As Talk Of MAS Policy Move Persists \b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 11:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar fell to a one-week low against the U.S. dollar Wednesday as talk of a possible policy shift by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July persisted, and amid a broadly stronger U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0915 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7365, compared with S$1.7328 late Tuesday in Asia. Intraday, it traded between S$1.7305 and S$1.7375, with the top end of the range being its highest level since early June. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar started the session around S$1.7328. But as the U.S. unit jumped to Y118.10 against the yen short covering was triggered, pushing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to S$1.7355. \par \par \uc2  After a brief dip to its session low, the U.S. unit resumed its ascent later in the session as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to trend higher against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the local market faced a dearth of fresh leads. \par \par \uc2  Market participants remained wary over recent speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weak and thereby aid the economy's flagging recovery. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the focus still seemed to be on data published by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore that showed foreign reserves rose US$2.44 billion in May from April, suggesting the MAS has been buying U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The sharp rise in the headline data has inevitably led to speculation that MAS was in the market last month, increasing the risk of some sort of change when MAS releases its biannual policy statement next month," United Overseas Bank said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  The MAS will issue its next policy statement in July, but for the time being market participants are watching for any hints as to whether it will change its current neutral policy bias. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, most dealers expect the local dollar to continue tracking direction in its regional counterparts, with the U.S. dollar likely to trade between S$1.7300 and S$1.7400 in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds recovered to close slightly higher Wednesday after five-sessions of losses as U.S. Treasury prices rose overnight, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But trade in the local bond market was moderate, with participants cautious ahead of a fresh 10-year government bond issue July 1. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore government is expected to auction between S$2 billion and S$2.5 billion of the 10-year bonds later this month, and market participants have been actively positioning for the issue in the past few weeks. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds slipped one basis point to 0.70%, while the yield on five-year bonds shed five basis points to 1.33%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds slipped four basis points to 1.77% and the yield on 10-year bonds fell three basis points to 1.99%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds ended two basis points lower at 2.42%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swap offers were also mostly lower\par as they tracked local bond yields in thin trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even news that national carrier Singapore Airlines Ltd. was planning\par to raise up to S$1 billion via a medium-term note program didn't cause a\par stir in the market, as details of the offer were still generally\par sketchy, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two-year swap offer fell three basis points to 0.86%, while the\par five-year offer fell four basis points to 1.49%. The 10-year offer\par inched one basis point lower to 2.30%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 144 basis points\par from 142 basis points late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady as liquidity\par remained sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.0625% 0.1875%   0.2500% 0.3750%\par 3-Month           0.5000% 0.6250%   0.5000% 0.6250%\par 1-Year            0.5625% 0.6875%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Simon Harvey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030611dz6b000kn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
