\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Step back with eye on yen, c.banks. \b0\par\par\uc2 768 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2003\par 11:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, June 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped back\par further from their recent highs on Monday, with the Singapore\par dollar, Thai baht and Taiwan dollar easing to their lowest\par levels in about a week before recouping some of their losses.\par     The Philippine peso        touched a two-month low amid\par speculation that more monetary easing was on its way, after\par last week's restoration of a system of decreasing interest\par rates for larger bank deposits at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Indonesian rupiah       , Asia's strongest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so\par far in 2003, also found it hard to push forward from around\par 8,200 per dollar. The market showed little response to the\par announcement of the widely expected sale of a controlling stake\par in Bank Danamon's (BDMN.JK) to Singapore's Temasek Holdings.\par For details click             .\par     Dealers in Jakarta said with the deal to be completed on\par June 16, the market would wait and see what dollar component of\par the sale hits the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The deal is estimated to be worth about $366 million, half\par of which would be in U.S. dollars. Some or all of this may have\par already been purchased in the market, dealers said. A bid bond\par of $15 million has already been paid by the Temasek consortium.\par     Overall sentiment in the region was guided by the U.S.\par dollar's rise against the yen  and euro       , and\par active resistance by some regional central banks to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength in recent days to protect export competitiveness,\par dealers said.\par     Philip Wee, treasury analyst at Singapore's DBS Bank, said\par investors were watching stock markets which had seen large\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows in recent weeks, such as Thailand.\par     "Some caution is likely as investors are looking for early\par warnings of any major correction as most Asian stock markets\par have risen quite a bit," he said.\par     Profit-taking in Thai stocks        , up 17 percent so far\par this year, added to the pressure on the baht . The baht\par was already easing from 10-month highs after the Bank of\par Thailand \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday to cap its rise and Governor\par Pridiyathorn Devakula had said he expected the baht to soften\par at some point.\par     The baht slipped to an early one-week low of 41.75 per\par dollar. It recovered a little, but was still well clear of the\par 10-month high around 41.40 hit on Thursday.\par     Wee said with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  clearly favouring a slightly\par weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , moves in the baht would be more dependent on\par swings in foreign portfolio investments.\par     PESO HITS 2-MONTH LOWS\par     Investors in the peso        were watching for clues to the\par next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  move on monetary policy.\par     Last week's restoration of the tiering rates system\par abolished in March was a de facto easing because it would boost\par liquidity.\par     The peso fell to 53.57 per dollar, its weakest since March\par 31. It pared some of those losses before the close, but dealers\par in Manila said the bias was still down.\par     Talk of easing and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  elsewhere worried investors\par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar, the region's most liquid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par Sing dollar drifted down to around 1.7300 per U.S. dollar,\par against last week's high of 1.7162, its strongest since May 15.\par     A mid-year policy review is due in early July from\par Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\par manages the exchange rate, its main monetary policy tool,\par against an undisclosed basket of trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Korean won            and Taiwan dollar          were\par supported by foreign investor inflows -- the won closed local\par trade at a two-week high -- but their respective central banks\par have been active in constraining any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength\par recently. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0846 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.39       117.85         -0.46\par  Sing dlr      1.7283       1.7239         -0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.660       34.639         -0.06\par  Korean won   1196.70      1200.30         +0.30\par  Baht           41.68        41.63         -0.12\par  Peso           53.38        53.45         +0.14\par  Rupiah       8180.00      8184.00         +0.05\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.39       118.74         +0.30\par  Sing dlr      1.7283       1.7341         +0.34\par  Taiwan dlr    34.660       34.753         +0.27\par  Korean won   1195.00      1185.80         -0.91\par  Baht           41.68        43.08         +3.36\par  Peso           53.38        53.38         +0.01\par  Rupiah       8180.00      8940.00         +9.29.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030609dz6900idb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
