\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht pulls back as c.bank steps up. \b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2003\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In SINGAPORE item headlined "Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -Baht pulls\par back as c.bank steps up", please read in 12th paragraph\par "...against the yen since May 1..." instead of "...against the\par yen this year..." (correcting reference period).\par     A corrected story follows.\par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , June 6 (Reuters) - Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled\par the Thai baht off 10-month highs on Friday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said he expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease.\par     Singapore dollar and Indonesian rupiah also eased from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  their highs and the Philippine peso slipped to a fresh \par \par \uc2  two-month low. Dealers said the underlying mood in regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was of caution ahead of crucial U.S. jobs data due \par \par \uc2  later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Regionals had strengthened after the dollar faltered on \par \par \uc2  some weak U.S. data, but their gains were restrained in morning \par \par \uc2  trade by caution about possible Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  which was fuelled by a series of government comments on the \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2  Korean markets were closed for a holiday on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht  eased to 41.66 per dollar, off a \par \par \uc2  10-month high of 41.41 hit in overnight New York trade, after \par \par \uc2  dealers in Bangkok said they spotted dollar bids from banks \par \par \uc2  that were usually active on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There were dollar bids, small but enough to let the market \par \par \uc2  know authorities don't want the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate any \par \par \uc2  further," said a dealer at a local bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The baht has gained about 3.5 percent against the dollar so \par \par \uc2  far this year, boosted by a rallying stock market and prospects \par \par \uc2  of strong growth driven by healthy domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Pridiyathorn Devakula, \par \par \uc2  said he expected the Thai baht to soften after its gains this \par \par \uc2  week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "It will soften later," he told reporters, without giving\par any timeframe.\par     When asked why he expected the baht to ease, Pridiyathorn\par said: "Because I say so."\par     Analysts said while the Bank of Thailand (BOT) has allowed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht to appreciate against the dollar on a nominal basis,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it has managed to keep the rise limited in trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par terms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sameer Goel, analyst at Bank of America in Singapore, said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht has gained only 1.9 percent against the yen since May\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1, and has declined 0.2 percent and 3.1 percent against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar and euro respectively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "BOT has also recently noted the possibility of core\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation undershooting its targets, and will be reluctant to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tighten monetary conditions through undue appreciation in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exchange rate," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the start of the week, the BOT held its benchmark 14-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repurchase rate steady at 1.75 percent, saying economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery has not generated any perceptible upward pressure on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PESO HITS TWO-MONTH LOW\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the Philippine peso  weakened in afternoon\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading to hit a two-month low of 53.46 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The easier tone in peso, which had lost about three percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since May 8 when it hit an eight-month high of 51.80, was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helped by an effective easing of monetary policy on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not cut official interest rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it did restore a tiered system of interest rates that pays\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks a decreasing rate on larger deposits held at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The step was a de facto easing as it would boost liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The tiered system was scrapped for a flat rate in March, when\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso was threatening record lows and money supply was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  edged back to around 1.7235 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar after rallying in New York trade to 1.7162, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strongest since May 15 when it hit a 33-month high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah , Asia's strongest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar this year, also stepped back to around 8,280\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar from Thursday's one-week high of 8,130.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0835 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.85       118.26         +0.35\par  Sing dlr      1.7239       1.7229         -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.639       34.665         +0.08\par  Baht           41.63        41.58         -0.12\par  Peso           53.45        53.33         -0.22\par  Rupiah       8184.00      8220.00         +0.44\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.85       118.74         +0.76\par  Sing dlr      1.7239       1.7341         +0.59\par  Taiwan dlr    34.639       34.753         +0.33\par  Baht           41.63        43.08         +3.48\par  Peso           53.45        53.38         -0.13\par  Rupiah       8184.00      8940.00         +9.24.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030606dz6600hlw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
