\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Stocks boost baht to 10-month high. \b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2003\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, June 3 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on\par Tuesday, led by the Thai baht  which hit a 10-month high,\par as the U.S. dollar eased against the closely watched yen\par  .\par     Sentiment on the dollar was hurt after the Group of Eight\par summit in France failed to discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates, bucking\par market expectations after some leaders had shown concern about\par the dollar's decline.\par  \par     The market was also unimpressed by President George W.\par Bush's support for a strong dollar.\par     "Nobody in the market really took him seriously," said Thio\par Chin Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors can now go back to chasing high yields\par without worrying about a coordinated G8 effort to help the weak\par dollar, analysts said.\par     However, fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  curb the yen's rise and reluctance to trade aggressively ahead \par \par \uc2  of Thursday's European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate meeting would \par \par \uc2  cap the upside for most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Recent data from across the region indicating slowing \par \par \uc2  exports was also likely to keep central banks on guard and keep \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains modest. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Rising portfolio investment by foreign investors was likely\par to remain the main driver of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength in the region.\par     The Thai baht        was propelled to a high of 41.51 per\par dollar, a level not seen since July 26, 2002, as portfolio\par inflows swelled.\par     Foreign investors were net buyers for the eleventh straight\par day on Monday of 734.22 million baht worth of Thai stocks,\par taking purchases to 8.38 billion baht so far this year.\par     Dealers in Bangkok said given the baht's high correlation\par to moves in the dollar/yen, the change of sentiment in the\par majors  exacerbated the move.\par     Portfolio inflows and hopes of more direct investment also\par pushed the Indonesian rupiah  to around 8,200 per dollar.\par     Indonesia's state-owned Bank Mandiri, the country's largest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank, said on Tuesday it planned an initial public offering of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 percent of the bank, with options to raise it to 15 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With foreign investors purchasing local stocks for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fifth consecutive day, the South Korean won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rose to 1,201.2 per dollar, from Monday's onshore close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,205.4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  firmed to 34.66 per U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the back of portfolio investment that had reached T$90\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in the past five weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect export competitiveness capped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        rose to 1.7224 per U.S. dollar,\par its strongest in about a week.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0852 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.63       118.44         -0.16\par  Sing dlr      1.7217       1.7294         +0.45\par  Taiwan dlr    34.682       34.691         +0.03\par  Korean won   1201.20      1205.40         +0.35\par  Baht           41.52        41.70         +0.43\par  Peso           53.16        53.25         +0.17\par  Rupiah       8230.00      8250.00         +0.24\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.63       118.74         +0.09\par  Sing dlr      1.7217       1.7341         +0.72\par  Taiwan dlr    34.682       34.753         +0.20\par  Korean won   1201.20      1185.80         -1.28\par  Baht           41.52        43.08         +3.76\par  Peso           53.16        53.38         +0.41\par  Rupiah       8230.00      8940.00         +8.63.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030603dz6300izu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
