\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Markets positioned for weaker dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2003\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, June 3 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  perked\par up early on Tuesday with the Thai baht, Singapore dollar and\par Indonesian rupiah near one-week highs, as players repositioned\par themselves for a weaker trend in the U.S. dollar.\par     The greenback was down against the yen        and lost\par ground against the euro  as the market was unimpressed by\par President George W. Bush's strong dollar policy rhetoric at the\par Group of Eight summit meeting in France.\par     Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities to curb the\par yen's rise and reluctance to trade aggressively ahead of\par Thursday's European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  interest rate meeting would\par cap the upside for most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     But the absence of wider discussion about the dollar at the\par Paris summit means \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors can go back to chasing\par high yields without worrying about a coordinated G8 effort to\par help the weak dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "For Asia it means more of the same," said Singapore-based\par emerging markets strategist David Simmonds at Royal Bank of\par Scotland.\par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to strengthen against the\par weak U.S. dollar but at the same slow and choppy pace we have\par seen so far this year," he said.\par     But recent indications of slowing exports from across the\par region and a clouded global demand outlook would keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gains modest, he added.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar        rose to 1.7242 per U.S. dollar\par and dealers said it might test last Wednesday's high of 1.7230.\par     The Thai baht        climbed to 41.56 per dollar, just shy\par of one-week high of 41.52, aided by rising portfolio investment\par by foreign investors.\par     Portfolio inflows and hopes of rising direct investments\par propelled the Indonesian rupiah  to around 8,200 per\par dollar.\par     Indonesia's state-owned Bank Mandiri, the country's largest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank, said on Tuesday it planned an initial public offering of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 percent of the bank, with options to raise it to 15 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With foreign investors purchasing local stocks for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fifth consecutive day, the South Korean won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rose to 1,202.1 per dollar, from Monday's onshore close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,205.4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  firmed to 34.66 per U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the back of portfolio investment that reached T$90 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the past five weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect export competitiveness might take some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shine off the Taiwan dollar's gains. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par AT 0256 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.38       118.44         +0.05\par  Sing dlr      1.7247       1.7294         +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.680       34.691         +0.03\par  Korean won   1202.30      1205.40         +0.26\par  Baht           41.51        41.70         +0.46\par  Peso           53.18        53.25         +0.13\par  Rupiah       8215.00      8250.00         +0.43\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.38       118.74         +0.30\par  Sing dlr      1.7247       1.7341         +0.55\par  Taiwan dlr    34.680       34.753         +0.21\par  Korean won   1202.30      1185.80         -1.37\par  Baht           41.51        43.08         +3.78\par  Peso           53.18        53.38         +0.38\par  Rupiah       8215.00      8940.00         +8.83.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030603dz63006y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
