\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Dn Late On Dlr's Overnight Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 1,157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2003\par 11:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly weaker Wednesday on the U.S. dollar's overnight gains, although they were off their intraday troughs as dollar selling re-emerged, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was, for the most part, range-bound, with no clear direction apparent. However the underlying sentiment for the dollar remains bearish, they noted. \par \par \uc2  "There's no trend. It's been rangy. It started with the dollar getting bid on short-covering because of the bounce overnight against the euro and yen," said a trader at a U.S. bank. But going into the latter part of the day, the dollar began to be sold off again, he said. \par \par \uc2  Given the weak dollar sentiment, the market expects more upside for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but players will remain vigilant of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The central banks would be there to smoothen the rise (of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," the trader said. He doesn't think the monetary authorities will try to reverse the upward trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The big trend is (for the) dollar (to go) down, so they probably can't fight that," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was barely changed from late Wednesday levels after hitting fresh 10-month highs in overnight trading. At 0900 GMT, the dollar was quoted around THB41.69 compared with THB41.68 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried to manage the Thai baht at an appropriate level amid the broad dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  "We did our best," he told reporters, but declined to say how much of dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought to cap the baht's strength. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn said huge capital inflows from foreign investors parking money in local stocks have also pushed up the baht recently. \par \par \uc2  "The high foreign reserves and seven straight days' of gains in Thai stocks show you how much (foreign) money is flowing into Thailand," he said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign net buying of Thai stocks so far this year totals THB4.77 billion. Thai foreign reserves stood at $38.8 billion as of May 16, up from $38.4 billion a week ago. \par \par \uc2  Also Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thailand's gross domestic product likely grew 6.3% in the first quarter of 2003 due to strong export growth and consumer demand but is expected to slow in coming quarters as a result of the SARS outbreak. \par \par \uc2  The Ministry is maintaining a 5.1% GDP growth forecast for 2003. If not for the SARS outbreak, 2003 growth would have exceeded last year's 5.2%, the ministry's fiscal policy office director Wisudhi Srisuphan said. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at S$1.7274 late in the local session, up from S$1.7240 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local dollar Tuesday also kept the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a stronger note, although analysts said there was little evidence to support the rumors. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, in a research note, said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't be justified as the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar wasn't anywhere near the limits of the policy band within which the local dollar is guided. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won closed above the 1,200 to the dollar mark for the first time in two weeks as the yen slipped against the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  Gains were partly offset by some dollar sales by exporters ahead of month-end settlements, market players said. Anticipated won buying by foreign stock funds that bought Korean shares recently also capped the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at KRW1,200.4, up from KRW1,198.6 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Investors have been wary about selling dollars in view of the South Korean government's commitment to support the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy said it will auction KRW1 trillion of five-year \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilization bonds June 3, which will equip authorities with more funds to boost the dollar if necessary. \par \par \uc2  The announcement came two days after the ministry's strong warning that the government will take action to curb the won's sharp rise. \par \par \uc2  "It's not that people are strongly interested in buying (the dollar) but they just can't sell (given the expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said a dealer at Chohung Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso closed at its weakest level in a month as banks covered short dollar positions in a shortened trading session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 53.10 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP52.88 Tuesday \par \par \uc2  Trading closed an hour early as heavy rains drenched the capital. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was closed after the government shut its offices as a result of flooding caused by typhoon Linfa. \par \par \uc2  A foreign bank trader said banks are now going long on the dollar as local interest rates start to decline due to huge liquidity in the financing system. \par \par \uc2  Treasury bill rates fell sharply at Monday's auction, with the yield on the benchmark 91-day treasury bill falling to 6.302% from 6.842% in the previous auction. \par \par \uc2  "The peso is correcting," the trader said. "Interest rates are becoming unattractive." \par \par \uc2  First-quarter economic growth data, which the government will issue early Thursday, however, may help support the peso, a local bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  The government is projecting growth in the first quarter to be around 4.6% on year, slightly better than market expectations of a 4.48% rise. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar ended at its lowest level in more than two weeks as the yen's fall encouraged short-covering in the U.S. unit, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Buying of U.S. dollars by importers and insurers also helped lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which closed at NT$34.730, its strongest close since May 9, and up from NT$34.712 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign banks bought U.S. dollars early in the session, pushing it to the intraday high of NT$34.740, after the government reported a 1% on-month decline in the April leading indicator. \par \par \uc2  However, U.S. dollar selling by exporters "gushed out in large amounts" in the afternoon, driving the unit to an intraday low of NT$34.708, said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying emerged again near the end of the session as banks covered short positions on the back of the yen's weakness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar often tracks the yen as Taiwan imports large amounts of goods from Japan and the two compete in some export categories. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah weakened slightly in choppy trading due to demand for dollars from importers and companies with foreign debt to repay by the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed the local session at 8,220 rupiah, up from IDR8,195 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030528dz5s000kk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
