\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk Supports USD \b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2003\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was weaker late Tuesday on U.S. dollar buying by a large local bank, sparking speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0820 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7240, up from S$1.7212 late Monday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7175 and S$1.7265 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened around S$1.7175 and drifted higher initially in line with its moves against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around midafternoon, the U.S. dollar spiked to S$1.7265 on buying by the large local bank, which some players believed was at the behest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The rise turned out to be brief, and the U.S. dollar slipped to S$1.7250 soon after as market participants took profit, suggesting the talk of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be true, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  An MAS spokeswoman wouldn't comment on the speculation when contacted by Dow Jones Newswires. "We do not comment on market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said. \par \par \uc2  "The rumors were going round, but they are generally not strong, just here and there," said an Asian bank dealer about the MAS' purported involvement. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's rise to its intraday high against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  coincided with its rise above Y117 against the yen, dealers added. The greenback has since come off that level and was changing hands at Y116.82 at the end of the Asian session. \par \par \uc2  Still, the fact that the stiff U.S. dollar buying emerged around S$1.7220 has been taken to mean the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not tolerate the U.S. dollar falling beyond that mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep between S$1.7220 and S$1.7270 in overnight trade later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were higher Tuesday, as market participants, facing a lack of leads due to the closure of U.S. Treasurys market overnight, focused on the weak domestic economic outlook, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bonds have resumed moving higher after a mild sell-off late last week drove prices down to very attractive levels, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations of further weakness in the domestic economic numbers in the coming months would allow Singapore Government Securities to remain well-bid in coming weeks," DBS Bank said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the yield on two-year bonds was two basis points lower at 0.69%, while the yield on five-year bonds also slipped two basis points to 1.31%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds also fell two basis points to 1.66% and the yield on 10-year bonds fell three basis points to 1.86%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds ended three basis points lower at 2.25%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, offers were also mostly lower as\par they tracked local bond yields. The two-year swap offer was one basis\par point lower at 0.88% while the five-year offer was three basis points\par lower at 1.44%. The 10-year offer slipped two basis points to 2.15%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed marginally to 127\par basis points from 128 basis points late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were steady as liquidity remained\par sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Tuesday      Late Monday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.5625% 0.6875%   0.5000% 0.5625%\par 3-Month           0.5000% 0.6250%   0.5000% 0.6250%\par 1-Year            0.5625% 0.6875%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Kevin Lim\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030527dz5r000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
