\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Surging rupiah nears 3-year highs. \b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2003\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, May 26 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah\par jumped to its strongest level in almost three years early on\par Monday, helped by speculation of investment inflows, and most\par other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also rose against a weakening U.S.\par dollar.\par     The rupiah rose to around 8,100 per U.S. dollar, a high\par since August 2000, powered by last week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments\par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not overvalued despite recent gains and\par could reach the 8,000 per dollar.\par     From a four-month low of 9,145 per dollar in March, the\par rupiah has surged about 12 percent, backed by global investors\par chasing high yields, the government's asset sales programme,\par and Jakarta's acceptance of a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     The military offensive against Aceh separatists has had\par little impact on the rupiah.\par     Last week, the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signalled it would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  give the green light for the sale of a 51 percent stake in Bank \par \par \uc2  Danamon (BDMN.JK) to Singapore's government investment agency, \par \par \uc2  Temasek Holdings, and Deutsche Bank (DBKGn.DE). The sale is \par \par \uc2  expected to raise around $350 million dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said most of the dollar sales on Monday \par \par \uc2  were from Singapore-based banks, while their was talk of some \par \par \uc2  flows related to the asset sales. \par \par \uc2  But a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta said trading \par \par \uc2  volume was just around $40 million in early hours, lending \par \par \uc2  support to views that the move was more sentiment driven. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He said the rupiah rise was exacerbated by stop-loss dollar\par sell orders triggered at 8,250 and then at around 8,200.\par     Analysts said that given the market was illiquid, only a\par small order was needed to push the rupiah higher.\par     "The asset sales picture is driving the rupiah, not so much\par the flow but the sentiment itself," said Craig Chan, analyst at\par Forecast Ltd.\par     Chan said depending on where Bank Indonesia steps in to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par curb the rise, the rupiah could touch 8,000 in the near-term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par before players reasses the risk of holding the rupiah. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah has not strengthened past 8,000 per dollar since May\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SUBDUED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, dealers expected trade would be subdued because\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets in both London and New York are closed for a holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Singapore dollar        rose to levels just shy of\par 1.7200 per dollar, from around 1.7230 in late Friday trade.\par     Given the sensitivity to moves in the dollar/yen       ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said the Singapore dollar was likely to be capped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.7180 on wariness of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen's rise against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht        rose to fresh nine-month highs at\par around 41.78 per dollar, from late Friday's 41.90.\par     Dealers said players were keeping an eye on any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves to cap baht's rise, even after the bank last week\par said the baht was competitive despite recent gains.\par     The Korean won                   opened at a 12-week high,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supported by expections of U.S. dollar sales towards the end of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the month. Still, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said any sharp gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could spark \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0323\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.85       117.25         +0.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7196       1.7227         +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr    34.681       34.707         +0.07\par  Korean won   1191.10      1194.40         +0.28\par  Baht           41.75        41.92         +0.41\par  Peso           52.79        52.79          0.00\par  Rupiah       8125.00      8275.00         +1.85\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.85       118.74         +1.62\par  Sing dlr      1.7196       1.7341         +0.84\par  Taiwan dlr    34.681       34.753         +0.21\par  Korean won   1191.10      1185.80         -0.44\par  Baht           41.75        43.08         +3.19\par  Peso           52.79        53.38         +1.12\par  Rupiah       8125.00      8940.00        +10.03.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030526dz5q0086u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
