\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Robust rupiah extends rally. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2003\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 21 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah's persistent rally took it to fresh 21-month highs on Wednesday, while the rest of the region kept to dull ranges after an offshore rally driven by the U.S. dollar's fall. \par \par \uc2  Most regionals were rangebound but strong, with the Singapore dollar stuck up a cent from late Tuesday, benefitting from the U.S. dollar's weakness after billionaire investor George Soros said he was selling the greenback. \par \par \uc2  Fears the Japanese authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen gains capped Asian regionals also. Additionally, worries over the rising cases of Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) hit the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht firmed past 42 per dollar to a nine-month high, and the Thailand \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still competitive and it was not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah, which is up 9.9 percent in two months, has shrugged off the military offensive against Aceh rebels and drew comfort from the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah's remark on Tuesday that the rupiah was still competitive. \par \par \uc2  "It's a combination of factors - a very weak dollar, very low U.S. interest rates and a decent yield on the rupiah," said David Simmonds, markets strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  But at Wednesday's high of 8,320, which is close to a technical resistance level at 8,300, traders were speculating the rally had to halt soon. \par \par \uc2  Exporters were aggressively selling their receivables in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , spot and future, and would soon be worried about losing competitiveness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Korean authorities effectively stalled the rallying won by hinting in an unusual manner at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The won paused near 1,193 per dollar after the finance ministry announced plans to issue won-denominated exchange stabilisation bonds soon. \par \par \uc2  "It seems to be a pre-emptive sterilisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Bhanu Baweja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with UBS Warburg, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The signal out here is that we are going to be issuing these bonds to sterilise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which means we are going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And, irrespective of whether they issue these bonds, I think they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the won's competitiveness." \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended stronger in light onshore trading, boosted by the yen's rally in offshore deals. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Malaysia unveiled a stimulus package to boost a slowing economy, cutting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by half a percentage point to 4.5 percent, boosting incomes and announcing plans for an increase in direct spending. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is pegged at 3.8 per U.S. dollar. On Tuesday, Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad had said there were no plans to move the ringgit peg down despite the dollar's weakness. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0850 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen 