\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah brushes aside Aceh, rest track. \b0\par\par\uc2 692 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2003\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In SINGAPORE story  headlined "Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -Rupiah\par  brushes aside Aceh, rest track yen" please read in final\par  paragraph "...the Malaysian economy on Wednesday." instead of\par  "...the Malaysian economy on Tuesday." (corrects day)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  A corrected story follows. \par \par \uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 20 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah bucked a regional bearish trend on Tuesday, resuming a rally it had halted last week as bullishness on improving fundamentals prevailed over the risks of the conflict with separatists in Aceh province. \par \par \uc2  On the second day of the Indonesian military offensive in Aceh, the rupiah  hit 8,360 per dollar, its strongest since August 2001 when it had rallied as far as 8,200 per dollar after Megawati Sukarnoputri became president. \par \par \uc2  In late trade, it pared some gains as traders booked profits but still ended up three-quarters of a percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  "It has been counter-intuitive and counter-trend. Either the market is overly complacent over the Aceh issue or the market is treating it as an internal security issue rather than a geopolitical flashpoint," said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  "And, it is fair to say that Aceh has been a long-standing situation and to a certain degree is an internal security issue," he said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has rallied 9.4 percent in two months, helped by the high yields Indonesian assets offer and the government's willingness to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  At his swearing in ceremony on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said the rupiah was still competitive. \par \par \uc2  Better than expected first-quarter GDP data on Monday helped prop up the rupiah as the U.S. dollar hit multi-year lows against the yen and euro on Monday, before talk of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the greenback off its lows. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's low correlation to other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also guarded it from the sell-off seen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the South African rand over the past week, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The attraction of the rupiah is that it has a low correlation with some of the high-yielders and with Asian markets in general, so it has just been left to its own devices," Piron said. \par \par \uc2  "But that is also symptomatic of the fact that it is an illiquid market and contains some restrictions in terms of foreign investment." \par \par \uc2  REST SHADOW YEN \par \par \uc2  The rest of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Tuesday, shadowing the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's two yen fall against the dollar from a two-year high on Monday of 115.10 per dollar on talk of sizeable Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar  was down more than a cent from Monday, dropping\par to the weak side of 1.73 per dollar and leading the fall in the Korean\par won                  , Philippine peso        and Thai baht       .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  was hurt by news the island had a record daily\par number of probable cases of Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) on\par Tuesday, as well as the weak yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Malaysia, Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said there were no plans\par to move the ringgit peg down from 3.80 per U.S. dollar despite the\par dollar's weakness. Mahathir is due to unveil a stimulus package for the\par Malaysian economy on Wednesday. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0820 GMT\par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     117.22       115.15         -1.77\par   Sing dlr      1.7315       1.7215         -0.58\par   Taiwan dlr    34.695       34.628         -0.19\par   Korean won   1198.60      1193.00         -0.47\par   Baht           42.11        41.95         -0.38\par   Peso           52.81        52.49         -0.61\par   Rupiah       8384.00      8448.00         +0.76\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     117.22       118.74         +1.30\par   Sing dlr      1.7315       1.7341         +0.15\par   Taiwan dlr    34.695       34.753         +0.17\par   Korean won   1198.60      1185.80         -1.07\par   Baht           42.11        43.08         +2.30\par   Peso           52.81        53.38         +1.08\par   Rupiah       8384.00      8940.00         +6.63.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030520dz5k00iiu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
