\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Following the fluctuating yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2003\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, May 13 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were tossed\par around by the yen  on Tuesday, challenging recent highs\par on signs U.S. authorities were not worried about a weaker\par dollar before snapping back on suspected Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar rose to around 1.7290 per U.S. dollar,\par a four-month high also hit overnight, but later eased back to\par the weaker side of 1.73 on talk the Bank of Japan was buying\par dollars as the yen seemed headed toward 116 per dollar.\par  \par     Against the euro, Singapore dollar rose to around 1.9875,\par off Monday's record lows beyond 2.01.\par     "The market is still focused on the dollar/yen," said a\par senior dealer at a local bank.\par     Dealers said the morning move towards the late January's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  highs was powered by some major funds buying Singapore dollars. \par \par \uc2  But rumours that local banks were buying dollars on behalf of \par \par \uc2  authorities helped reverse the market's direction. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said central banks across the region were \par \par \uc2  targeting exchange rate stability to protect export \par \par \uc2  competitiveness. Many Asia countries compete against each \par \par \uc2  other in export markets and do not want strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  make their exports expensive. \par \par \uc2  "Unless the Bank of Japan is seen easing its grip on the \par \par \uc2  yen, central banks in Asia will be sensitive to any sharp \par \par \uc2  move," said Philip Wee, treasury strategist at Singapore's DBS \par \par \uc2  Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan was cited by traders as a dollar buyer \par \par \uc2  after the yen had strengthened on U.S. Treasury Secretary John \par \par \uc2  Snow's comments to Reuters that Japan and Europe should not \par \par \uc2  blame a weaker dollar for their economic woes. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN RATE CUT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht eased to around 42.46 per dollar from \par \par \uc2  two-month highs of 42.29 hit in offshore trade. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers in Bangkok said foreign banks were spotted buying\par dollars, but local players supported the baht on the downside.\par     Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also kept the South Korean won\par around 1,200 per dollar. A widely expected 25 basis point\par interest rate cut by the Bank of Korea had little impact.\par     Wee said the BOK's concerns about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength to\par protect exports and economic growth were no different from\par other regional central banks.\par     Korean government bonds rallied as traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had not ruled out the possibility of further cuts.\par     The Indonesian rupiah ran into profit-taking after rallying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past 8,400 per dollar for the first time since August 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said overall sentiment was still positive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after Monday's upgrade by Standard and Poor's.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso tested 52 per dollar, but dealers in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manila said the softness in other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar kept the peso from breaching the level. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0850 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.12       116.49         -0.54\par  Sing dlr      1.7325       1.7326         +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.717       34.710         -0.02\par  Korean won   1199.50      1195.40         -0.34\par  Baht           42.36        42.35         -0.02\par  Peso           52.16        52.05         -0.21\par  Rupiah       8438.00      8430.00         -0.09\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.12       118.74         +1.38\par  Sing dlr      1.7325       1.7341         +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    34.717       34.753         +0.10\par  Korean won   1199.50      1185.80         -1.14\par  Baht           42.36        43.08         +1.70\par  Peso           52.16        53.38         +2.28\par  Rupiah       8438.00      8940.00         +5.95.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030513dz5d00izi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
