\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Knocked by euro,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  risk. \b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 11:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , May 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could not\par rise against a troubled U.S. dollar on Friday because traders\par feared \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect exports, and they weakened\par sharply against the euro as it surged to a record high against\par the yen.\par     Dealers blamed the snap in the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rally on\par the yen. Worries, and threats, about Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw\par it pull back from Wednesday's 10-month highs near 116 per\par dollar, and it also hit a life low against the euro.\par     That move weakened the Singapore dollar past 2.0 per euro\par to its lowest against the single European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since its\par launch in January 1999.\par     Dealers and analysts believe most Asian central banks had\par been buying dollars in recent sessions to protect export\par competitiveness in the key U.S. market, and this had triggered\par profit-taking that kept regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  off their highs.\par     Against the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar, the Singapore dollar, Thai baht,\par Korean won and the Taiwan dollar all held below two-month highs\par hit after the Federal Reserve had warned about the risk of\par deflation on Tuesday.\par  \par     "Asia is quasi-pegged against the yen," said Ray Farris,\par Credit Suisse First Boston's strategist in Singapore.\par     "They (Asian central banks) are quasi-pegging against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, so if euro/yen goes higher, euro/Asia goes higher, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they are doing that essentially to ensure that their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted indices are stable or depreciating," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar and South Korean won have lost about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.4 percent and 1.2 percent respectively against the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar so far this year, but against the euro their losses are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about 11 percent each in the same period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even the high yielding Philippine peso and Indonesian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah, which have gained about two percent and 4.7 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par respectively against the dollar, have lost some 7.5 and 4.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent of value against the euro this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said those losses against the euro showed that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while some Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have gained against the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the overall trade-weighted performances was not as strong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW LOW\par     The euro/Sing cross traded as high as 2.0088 on Friday.\par     Dealers said the trade has gained popularity in recent days\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the euro, along with the yen and U.S dollar, was a major\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par component of the undisclosed trade-weighted index the Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manages the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I suspect part of this story is the euro/yen game or the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar trade against its (trade weighted) basket," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Simon Flint, strategist at Bank of America in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said players who had been recently taking a bullish view\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the Sing dollar against the basket \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , on the back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of U.S. dollar weakness, had been hit by the euro's persistent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some dealers said the pullback from two-month highs against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. dollar may also have contributed to some players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taking what seems to be a safer bet - short Sing dollar and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar weakened past 1.74 per dollar late on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday, having avoided Wednesday's high of 1.7365 in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht fell to around 42.60 per dollar before paring\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some of the losses, but it remained clear of this week's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-month high around 42.40.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso eased to around 52.41 per dollar, a day after it\par hit 51.88, its strongest since September 13 last year.\par     The Indonesian rupiah rose back to Thursday's 11-month high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 8,495, after hitting an intraday low of 8,600. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. DOLLAR AT 0801 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.29       116.35         -0.80\par  Sing dlr      1.7406       1.7381         -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.773       34.716         -0.16\par  Korean won   1200.10      1199.00         -0.09\par  Baht           42.55        42.44         -0.26\par  Peso           52.34        52.15         -0.36\par  Rupiah       8540.00      8555.00         +0.18\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.29       118.74         +1.24\par  Sing dlr      1.7406       1.7341         -0.37\par  Taiwan dlr    34.773       34.753         -0.06\par  Korean won   1200.10      1185.80         -1.19\par  Baht           42.55        43.08         +1.25\par  Peso           52.34        53.38         +1.94\par  Rupiah       8540.00      8940.00         +4.68.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz5900i21\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
