\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Gains checked by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2003\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Ovais Subhani\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , May 8 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso pulled\par back from an eight-month high and the Indonesian rupiah pared\par its rally to an 11-month peak on Thursday as suspected\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stalled the regional slide in the U.S. dollar.\par The Singapore dollar, Thai baht and Taiwan dollar edged\par back from two-month highs as the Japanese talked the yen down\par from 10-month highs near 116 yen.\par Dealers said suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by several Asian\par central banks, to cap \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and protect export\par competitiveness, had prompted some closing of short dollar\par positions.\par Korean financial markets were closed for a holiday.\par "Asian being an export-oriented region, the central banks\par here have an incentive to try and stem any rapid appreciation\par in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as the recovery in the U.S. and global\par economy is still very uncertain," Bank of America analyst\par Sameer Goel said.\par The peso ended local trade at 52.15 per dollar after\par opening at 51.88, its strongest since September 13 last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It has risen about six percent since mid-March, when it was\par above 55 per dollar and targetting record lows.\par Dealers in Manila said remittances from overseas workers\par for the school admission season in May had helped the peso.\par An added boost came from the weak dollar and the search for\par higher yield by investors, overshadowing worries about ratings\par downgrades and large budget deficits.\par But talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity pushed the peso to the\par weaker side of 52 per dollar in afternoon trade.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said the peso\par should hold steady around current levels.\par "This is the rate we always thought it should be if we did\par not have the extraneous factors," he said after the bank left\par its official rates unchanged at its meeting on Thursday.\par Another Asian high yielder, the Indonesian rupiah, rallied\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 8,495 per dollar, its strongest since June 2002, even as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benchmark interest rates eased. But talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying dollars pulled it back to around 8,550.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rate on one-month Bank Indonesia paper fell to 10.91\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent at Wednesday's auction from 11.06 percent last week,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while three-month paper fell to 10.89 percent from 11.29 last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers said the rupiah, which has risen about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seven percent since March, was still attractive as interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates would be double-digit for some time.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll this week found an average forecast of 10.28\par percent for the benchmark one-month paper by the end of 2003.\par SARS RISK UNWOUND\par The Singapore dollar stayed close to a two-month high of\par 1.7365 per U.S. dollar, but was wary of further gains.\par Dealers said the weak U.S. dollar and a market view the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deadly SARS virus, which killed 27 people on the island, was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par under control had prompted an unwinding of the SARS risk\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par premium priced into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during March and April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the Sing was checked by the steadier dollar and\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears after dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have checked rates with local banks on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday - seen as a warning against sharp \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht held a 42.40-42.44 per dollar range amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspicion the Bank of Thailand was buying dollars for a second\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said a desire to avoid triggering stop-loss\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-sell orders lined beyond 42.40 also helped cap the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0830 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par Japan yen     116.35       117.48         +0.97\par Sing dlr      1.7381       1.7429         +0.28\par Taiwan dlr    34.716       34.712         -0.01\par Baht           42.44        42.55         +0.26\par Peso           52.15        52.07         -0.15\par Rupiah       8555.00      8530.00         -0.29\par Change on year\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par Japan y