\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly up but Sing dlr eases on virus. \b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2003\par 06:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, April 1 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar\par tripped off one-week highs early on Tuesday amid further signs\par that the outbreak of a killer virus in Asia was affecting\par sentiment.\par  \par     Most other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were pushed higher by the\par U.S. dollar's weakness against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     However, gains were slim. War in Iraq, tensions in North\par Korea and recent economic data both in the region and outside\par have weighed on sentiment.\par     The Singapore dollar eased to around 1.7670 per dollar from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Monday's one-week high of 1.7623 following news that the killer \par \par \uc2  virus - Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) - claimed \par \par \uc2  its fourth victim in the island-state on Monday. Schools in the \par \par \uc2  city have been shut and 945 people quarantined. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said the impact of the outbreak, that has \par \par \uc2  also killed people in Hong Kong, Vietnam and China, had been \par \par \uc2  muted so far in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "Equity markets in Asia suffered huge losses overnight as \par \par \uc2  players worried about the impact of SARS virus on economic \par \par \uc2  growth, but this has thus far not found sympathy from the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  markets," said Bhanu Baweja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS \par \par \uc2  Warburg. \par \par \uc2  Singapore-based Baweja said several economies in the region \par \par \uc2  risked growth downgrades if the outbreak hit the region's \par \par \uc2  multibillion dollar tourism industry. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said some caution in pushing the Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar higher was also due to speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  authorities might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht  held steady at around 42.85 per dollar \par \par \uc2  as players positioned for lower U.S. dollar and yen demand from \par \par \uc2  local corporates and importers, with their month-end needs \par \par \uc2  already covered in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso  rose to 53.30 per dollar from \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's onshore close of 53.52 as dollar sales by a foreign \par \par \uc2  bank sparked rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said high volumes gave some credence to the \par \par \uc2  rumours. Some $59.5 million worth of business was transacted in \par \par \uc2  the first couple of hours, surpassing the $59 million traded in \par \par \uc2  the whole of Monday. \par \par \uc2  "No one is sure, but some of the dollar supply had been \par \par \uc2  coming from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions," a dealer at a \par \par \uc2  local bank in Manila said. \par \par \uc2  Banks in Philippines have been dumping their long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions after eight of them were penalised by authorities for \par \par \uc2  violating regulations last week. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah  was slightly weaker but still \par \par \uc2  within familiar range around the 8,900 to the dollar level as \par \par \uc2  some offshore players were spotted covering short-dollar \par \par \uc2  positions. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0325 GMT \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.27       118.88         +0.52\par  Sing dlr      1.7659       1.7631         -0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.755       34.750         -0.01\par  Korean won   1253.10      1254.60         +0.12\par  Baht           42.84        42.86         +0.05\par  Peso           53.32        53.52         +0.38\par  Rupiah       8903.00      8900.00         -0.03\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.27       118.74         +0.40\par  Sing dlr      1.7659       1.7341         -1.80\par  Taiwan dlr    34.755       34.753         -0.01\par  Korean won   1253.10      1185.80         -5.37\par  Baht           42.84        43.08         +0.56\par  Peso           53.32        53.38         +0.11\par  Rupiah       8903.00      8940.00         +0.42.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030401dz41008ce\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
