\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won's woes multiply, peso plunges. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 12 (Reuters) - The Korean won led the pack of weakening Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday after an accounting scandal spurred an onslaught on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which was already pressured by persistent geopolitical risks. The Philippines was the other weak spot in the region. The peso dropped as low as 55.10 per dollar, a fresh 26-month low. \par \par \uc2  The weakness in these two overshadowed the Singapore dollar's slide to a three-week low as the yen and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceded ground to a U.S. dollar benefitting from Washington's delay of a U.N. vote on military action against Iraq. \par \par \uc2  SK GROUP SCANDAL HURTS WON \par \par \uc2  Traders said the unearthing of a $1.2 billion accounting scandal at Korea's fourth biggest conglomerate SK Group hurt all Korean markets. Stocks fell to a 17-month low, the won ended onshore trade at a five-month low of 1,245, credit swap spreads widened, and bonds fell sharply. \par \par \uc2  The won market even disregarded warnings by authorities and some suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state banks. \par \par \uc2  Even an assurance by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it was considering providing funds to financial companies to stabilise the markets did not calm the won. \par \par \uc2  "Markets are beginning to realise that what looked a couple of months ago like a story that was rosy on all fronts for Korea now looks exactly the opposite," said James Malcolm, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with JP Morgan. \par \par \uc2  "You have got global and local geopolitical risks, a new government that seems to be messing up everything they touch, such as bilateral relations with the U.S., the corporate sector." \par \par \uc2  And, because the authorities had been slow in voicing concern over the moves, bearishness had been amplified, he said. \par \par \uc2  Additionally, a tolerable cost of carrying a short won position and a still not-so-steep forward curve implied there would be no hurry to unwind short won positions, Malcolm said. \par \par \uc2  The SK Group scandal took some attention away from tensions over North Korea's nuclear plans and missile tests, which had been bothering the won, amid reports of further deployment of U.S. warplanes in the South. \par \par \uc2  Bank of America said in its commentary on Wednesday the Korean authorities may be quite content with a weakening won. \par \par \uc2  "The policy preference during a weakening economy would likely be a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The discomfort is probably due to the sharp move. We stay won negative," it said. \par \par \uc2  PESO'S SLOW ROUT \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at its third 26-month low in as many days this week as demand for dollars from oil companies building up their reserves before a likely Gulf war continued. But other fundamental and technical reasons were also working against it. \par \par \uc2  For one, the steep drop has brought the peso close to its historic low of 55.75, hit in volatile trade in January 2001 as President Joseph Estrada was being forced from office, which puts it into uncharted territory where there are were no technical barriers. \par \par \uc2  Fundamentally, last week's bombings in the southern Philippines only added to the peso's woes, which include rising oil prices, a growing budget deficit, and uncertainty over whether its new anti-money laundering laws would be approved by the Paris-based Financial Action Task Force. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco told reporters the peso was affected by war jitters. \par \par \uc2  "As soon as this source of uncertainty is over, peso should recover," he said. \par \par \uc2  RUPIAH, BAHT FOLLOW \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht followed the Sing dollar, with traders reporting some short positions in both these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  being squeezed out as they fell. \par \par \uc2  But analysts also pointed to the consistent sales of Thai stocks by foreign investors in the past week. \par \par \uc2  Analysts dismissed market speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) to push the Sing dollar down, saying even at its highest it had been within the undisclosed trade-weighted band authorities manage it in. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar finally succumbed to the weakness in neighbouring Korea and fell to a one-week low. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah fell only slightly. Markets were paying close attention to the varying news of asset sales by the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA). \par \par \uc2  A Singapore-led consortium is leading a bid for a stake in Bank Danamon, but IBRA also said it would halt the restructuring of Asia Pulp & Paper's Indonesian debts until creditors clarified a letter sent to the country's president. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0901 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     117.45       117.21         -0.20\par   Sing dlr      1.7457       1.7364         -0.53\par   Taiwan dlr    34.721       34.620         -0.29\par   Korean won   1242.60      1229.90         -1.02\par   Baht           42.67        42.44         -0.54\par   Peso           55.09        54.90         -0.34\par   Rupiah       8891.00      8880.00         -0.12\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     117.45       118.74         +1.10\par   Sing dlr      1.7457       1.7341         -0.66\par   Taiwan dlr    34.721       34.753         +0.09\par   Korean won   1242.60      1185.80         -4.57\par   Baht           42.67        43.08         +0.96\par   Peso           55.09        53.38         -3.10\par   Rupiah       8891.00      8940.00         +0.55.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030312dz3c00jas\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
