\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Constrained by N.Korea, c.banks. \b0\par\par\uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2003\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw little benefit from a weakening U.S. dollar on Friday as tensions over North Korea's nuclear programme and concerns regional central banks will not let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate weighed them down. \par \par \uc2  Traders said foreign investment and fund houses were seen picking up dollars against the regionals. \par \par \uc2  "The North Korean issue is standing in the way of regionals (firming)," a Singapore-based chief dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "We can see all these funds picking up the dollar against Asians, and they are probably quite right in betting that even if the dollar falls a lot, the regional central banks will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar  visited lows near 1.76 again in offshore deals, but was higher at 1.7530/40 by the time Asian trading started. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             also managed to withstand another bear\par attack that took it past 1,206, and was back hugging the 1,200 level in\par morning trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Markets remained jittery over the North Korean standoff, despite the\par United States saying it is not seeking sanctions against the country,\par which Pyongyang has said it would view as a declaration of war. On\par Wednesday, North Korea was declared in breach of the United Nation's\par atomic safeguards and the matter was referred to the U.N. Security\par Council.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar held its ground against the yen  around 120.40, after a\par half percent fall on Thursday amid worries over terror attacks and the\par approaching deadline for the U.N. arms inspectors' report on Iraq.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian markets also worried about oil prices at 28-month highs and about\par how far the Japanese authorities would let the yen rise before\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while they waited for the Bank of Japan to end a two-day\par policy meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The National Australia Bank said in its weekly report it expected the\par dollar to be supported in Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Throughout the next few weeks we should expect Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par generally to trade at the lower end of recent ranges as the current\par macro environment is not conducive to growth assets, the North Korean\par crisis has further in which to run, and secondly the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has engaged in a concerted effort to weaken the yen," it\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BEARISHNESS WIDESPREAD\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All the major Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were flat or marginally up from\par Thursday's levels, while the Thai baht and the Indonesian rupiah were\par the only ones stronger from the end of 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But traders said the baht  has limited room to appreciate, given\par expectations the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will use any regional downtrend to buy\par dollars as the early repayment of IMF loans begins.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, Thailand repays $950 million of an IMF-arranged loan,\par leaving $3.85 billion outstanding. The government intends to clear the\par loans by July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar will stay under pressure until strong evidence of\par economic recovery emerges, given its open economy and susceptibility to\par global trends, traders said. Analysts said it had however moved into\par the lower half of the undisclosed trade-weighted band that authorities\par manage it in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Sing dollar is now at the weaker half of the NEER band. Besides\par euro's strength, this is largely due to dollar/Sing downside limited by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears, increasing geopolitical tensions and the domestic\par economy in a bad shape," United Overseas Bank said in a market note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WON'S RESPITE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar's woes gave the Korean won some respite, despite its\par proximity to North Korea. It held around 1,200 even as the country's\par main stock index  hitting a 15-month low, with foreigners among thoses\par selling stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier this week, Moody's Investors Service downgraded its outlook on\par South Korea's A3 rating to negative.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But on Thursday, ratings agency Fitch said it expected a diplomatic\par resolution to the crisis, said South Korea's economic fundamentals\par leave it well placed to withstand even a prolonged period of heightened\par tension. Fitch has an A rating on South Korea.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  recovered from Thursday's close at 53.95, marking\par time as traders braced for further weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It struck a 18-month low of 54.10 per dollar last week, from where it\par was pulled away by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warnings on dollar hoarding and some\par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0340 GMT Change on\par the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     120.48       120.83         +0.29\par   Sing dlr      1.7534       1.7547         +0.07\par   Taiwan dlr    34.817       34.817         +0.00\par   Korean won   1201.00      1202.30         +0.11\par   Baht           43.01        43.01         +0.00\par   Peso           53.89        53.95         +0.11\par   Rupiah       8935.00      8942.00         +0.08\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     120.48       118.74         -1.44\par   Sing dlr      1.7534       1.7341         -1.10\par   Taiwan dlr    34.817       34.753         -0.18\par   Korean won   1201.00      1185.80         -1.27\par   Baht           43.01        43.08         +0.16\par   Peso           53.89        53.38         -0.95\par   Rupiah       8935.00      8940.00         +0.06.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030214dz2e006n0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
