\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late, In Tight Band; USD Bias Still Weak \b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2003\par 09:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar strengthened against its U.S. counterpart Wednesday, but stayed in a tight trading range, as uncertainty over the prospects of a U.S.-led war with Iraq continued to plague market sentiment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7380, down from S$1.7412 late Tuesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7375 and S$1.7390 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened around S$1.7380 in Asia after retreating overnight against its regional rivals, particularly the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It briefly rose early in the session, but slipped back to S$1.7375 midmorning and then spent the rest of the session trading around that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants continued to look for levels to sell the U.S. dollar and take profit following gains chalked up since Friday. \par \par \uc2  Overall market sentiment was still generally uncertain, especially ahead of U.S. Secretary of State Colin Powell's address to the U.N. later Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  His address is expected to give the markets a clearer view of geopolitical developments, particularly with regard to possible strikes against Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Until market participants obtain a better picture of what the U.S. plans to do, most expect the U.S. dollar to continue to be pressured, though concerns over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary authorities may keep the falls limited, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will find immediate support at S$1.7370, its intraday low for the past two global sessions, with resistance at S$1.7430. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds rose sharply Wednesday sparked by an overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys, as concerns over the possibility of war and global economic uncertainties continued to favor sentiment toward lesser-risk bonds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, most bond yields were hovering near their historic lows, as the local market remained flush with liquidity and funding costs remain cheap, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "This is uncharted territory," a foreign bank dealer said, "The (banking) system still has a lot of funds." \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds ended three basis points lower at 0.91%, while the yield on five-year bonds was down one basis point at 1.56%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds fell four basis points to 1.88%, while the yield on 10-year bonds shed five basis points to 2.37%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds fell seven basis points to end at 2.73%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swap offers also fell to all-time\par lows as they tracked local bond yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two-year swap offer ended two basis points lower at 1.13%, while\par the five-year swap offer fell three basis points to 1.80%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 10-year offer fell six basis points to 2.45%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 132 basis points\par from 136 basis points late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mixed, as the overnight rate\par came off its early low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.1875% 0.3125%   0.1250% 0.2500%\par 3-Month           0.6250% 0.7500%   0.6250% 0.7500%\par 1-Year            0.7500% 0.8750%   0.8125% 0.9375%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030205dz25000hs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
