\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Worried about war, oil,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2003\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 29 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose off their lows on Wednesday as U.S. President George W. Bush said "crucial hours may lie ahead" for U.S. forces in the Gulf, but their gains were limited by concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rising oil prices. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar saw the largest swings, weakening in New York after U.S. Treasury Secretary designate John Snow affirmed the strong U.S. dollar policy and then started rising ahead of Bush's State of the Union address. The Sing dollar hit a high of 1.7285 per U.S. dollar and then settled around 1.73. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar weakened on rumours that Bush would declare war during his speech. He did not, but vowed to use the full force of the U.S. military to disarm Iraq if necessary, which kept the U.S. dollar on the defensive. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah also benefitted, rising past a key resistance at 8,850 and leaving behind a week-long range around 8,890. \par \par \uc2  Another bout of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the Korean won reined in around 1,170, helped by the yen's resistance to rallying too far past 118 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso fell to a two-month low of 53.82 per dollar after the government, in preparation for any Gulf war, activated an oil contingency plan requiring refiners to maintain a minimum 30-day inventory of crude and products by February 3. \par \par \uc2  "The peso's fall is demand-driven. Oil companies have been asked to beef up their reserves and have been buying dollars," said Rovic De Guzman, head of trading at Union Bank of the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was wedged in a 42.60-42.68 range by the rising war risks, as well as suspicion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was continuously mopping up the heavy influx of foreign investments. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have been net buyers of 7.8 billion baht of Thai stocks so far this year, over half the 14.34 billion baht they bought in all of 2002. \par \par \uc2  Traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is accumulating dollar reserves to facilitate the proposed early prepayment of some $4.8 billion on IMF loans by mid-2003. \par \par \uc2  WAITING FOR EVENTS \par \par \uc2  Traders said Bush's speech suggested the United States could take unilateral action to force Iraq to disarm, yet markets would wait for signals from Bush's meeting on Friday with British Prime Minister Tony Blair and U.S. Secretary of State Colin Powell's presentation on Iraq to the United Nations on February 5. \par \par \uc2  In a commentary, Bank of America said Bush's speech was sufficiently hawkish to suggest the United States would not waver in its resolve to disarm Iraq, and, by flagging Powell's U.N. appearance, appeared to accelerate the timetable for war. \par \par \uc2  Bhanu Baweja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with UBS Warburg, said the bearishness on the dollar would persist until Powell's presentation next week. \par \par \uc2  "He (Bush) hasn't set any deadlines, but the dollar's not coming off. Fundamentally, even at current high levels of short dollar positioning, the market does not want to take profits," said Baweja. \par \par \uc2  "The probability of war is unchanged. The market is basically just switching its focus from January 29 to February 5," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0859 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.15       118.80         +0.55\par   Sing dlr      1.7303       1.7311         +0.05\par   Taiwan dlr    34.643       34.660         +0.05\par   Korean won   1170.00      1170.30         +0.03\par   Baht           42.64        42.69         +0.12\par   Peso           53.75        53.73         -0.04\par   Rupiah       8850.00      8880.00         +0.34\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.15       118.74         +0.50\par   Sing dlr      1.7303       1.7341         +0.22\par   Taiwan dlr    34.643       34.753         +0.32\par   Korean won   1170.00      1185.80         +1.35\par   Baht           42.64        43.08         +1.03\par   Peso           53.75        53.38         -0.69\par   Rupiah       8850.00      8940.00         +1.02.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030129dz1t00hwp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
