\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late, Broad USD Falls; Mkt Ignores Data \b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2003\par 09:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was stronger late Monday as market participants continued to hold their weak outlook for the U.S. dollar, but ignored better-than-expected Singapore industrial output data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0820 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7278, down from S$1.7310 late Friday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7265 and S$1.7298 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened around S$1.7270, after recovering from its sharp plunge to S$1.7235, its lowest since late 2000, during the New York trading session Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  That was also well below the 2002 low of S$1.7260 against the local dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar extended its rise from early in the session, mainly because some market participants were concerned that the sharp U.S. dollar fall would draw \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rise was halted around midday but resumed late in the session, though sporadic sell on rally trades caused it to slip several times through the local session. \par \par \uc2  Overall market sentiment for the U.S. unit was largely negative, but market participants are hoping for a better picture of how the U.S. might act against Iraq after U.N. weapons inspectors issue a key report on their work later Monday. \par \par \uc2  With market attention intently focused on external developments, Singapore dealers generally ignored the issue of December industrial output data, which showed production rising by a better-than-expected 19% year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  This beat the average forecast of a 8.9% rise by seven economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  The data also suggests that a double-dip recession in the fourth quarter of last year can be effectively ruled out, economists said. \par \par \uc2  All this failed to inspire the market, though, with the U.S. dollar hovering around S$1.7280 before and after the data was issued. \par \par \uc2  Later Monday, dealers expect the U.S. dollar to keep to a similar range against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a slew of events scheduled this week, including the weapons inspectors' report, President George W. Bush's State of the Union address, and the Federal Open Market Committee meeting. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar will find support at S$1.7230 with resistance at S$1.7300. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were modestly higher late Monday as fears of a war in the Middle east fueled buying in instruments deemed safer than equities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But overall trade in the local bond market was generally quiet, as participants waited for direction from the U.S. Treasury's market once the weapons inspectors' report on Iraq is issued. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the yields on two- and five-year bonds were three basis points lower at 1.03% and 1.60%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was four basis points lower at 2.01%, while the yield on 10-year bonds slipped three basis points to 2.52%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds ended two basis points lower at 2.92%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swap offers tracked local bond\par yields lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two-year swap offer ended one basis point lower at 1.21%, while\par the five-year swap offer fell two basis points to 1.91%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 10-year offer slipped four basis points to 2.60%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was narrower at 139 basis\par points, from 143 basis points late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, although the\par overnight rates inched higher, while overall liquidity remained\par sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Monday       Late Friday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.6250% 0.7500%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par 3-Month           0.6875% 0.8125%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 1-Year            0.8125% 0.9375%   0.8125% 0.9375%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030127dz1r000ip\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
