\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Steady Late;US Dlr Retreats From Early High \b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2003\par 10:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was steady late Thursday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated from a modest overnight rebound against its Asian counterparts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7326, little changed from S$1.7322 late Wednesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7320 and S$1.7352 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar kick-started the Asian session around S$1.7340, and subsequently bumped up to S$1.7350 as it rode on its overnight rebound against its Asian rivals, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But as with the past few sessions, the greenback failed to hang on to its gains. Market participants trimmed their U.S. dollar positions and took profit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the halfhearted rebound partly to the U.S. dollar's inability to break above Y119 against the yen. By the end of the Asian session, the U.S. dollar was trading at Y118.24 after meeting resistance at Y118.80 intraday. \par \par \uc2  Worries that a U.S.-led strike on Iraq was inevitable ensued in very bearish sentiment on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But concerns over the domestic economic outlook and potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also limited the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the U.S. dollar to continue to drift lower toward end-week, with the U.S. dollar remaining at risk from another round of selling upon new adverse developments on the Iraqi warfront," United Overseas Bank said in a research report Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "That said, markets are probably waiting for the first shot to be fired before reversing current risk aversion trades," UOB added. \par \par \uc2  Near-term, the U.S. dollar is likely to continue to come under pressure, with support pegged at S$1.7300, while any resistance would likely be around S$1.7360-65, its highest level so far this week. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly lower late Thursday as market participants ignored the overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys and took profit on the healthy gains this week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some market players also adjusted positions on news the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore would auction S$1 billion worth of government bonds on Jan. 29, which pushed bond prices lower. \par \par \uc2  The bonds, maturing February 2005, are a reopening of an older five-year issue and carry a 4.00% coupon. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the yield on two-year bonds was one basis point lower at 1.05%, while the yield on five-year bonds was up four basis points at 1.66%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was six basis points higher at 2.11%, while the yield on 10-year bonds also gained six basis points to 2.60%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds ended eight basis points higher at 2.99%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swap offers mostly tracked local\par bond yields,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two- and five-year swap offers both rose two basis points each to\par 1.23% and 1.96%, respectively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 10-year offer rose three basis points to 2.66%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was wider at 143 basis\par points, from 142 basis points late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, although the\par overnight rates inched higher. Overall liquidity remained sufficient in\par the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Thursday     Late Wednesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.5000% 0.6250%   0.1875% 0.2500%\par 3-Month           0.6875% 0.8125%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 1-Year            0.8750% 1.0000%   0.8750% 1.0000%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030123dz1n000jy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
