\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Trapped by growth and war risks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2003\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a relatively quiet Thursday in the midst of volatile major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pinned by worries over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , higher oil prices and tensions of war on Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, Korean won and other regionals softened in the morning as the yen remained wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and then settled into tight ranges ahead of the January 27 deadline for U.N. inspectors to submit their report on Iraq's weapons. Markets were also uneasy ahead of next week's State of the Union address by U.S. President George. W. Bush, after he stepped up the war rhetoric recently, and U.S. Treasury Secretary nominee John Snow's Senate hearing. \par \par \uc2  The dollar extended its recovery against the yen to over 118.70/80 and then fell back. But the euro struck fresh 3-= year highs against the yen, boosted by safe-haven flows. \par \par \uc2  Frank Gong, head of Asian markets strategy at Bank of America, said the euro was the biggest beneficiary of the dollar's weakness and the fear of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to weaken the yen was weighing on the latter. \par \par \uc2  "The yen seems to be the weakest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dog of all the G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the euro is the star, and traders continue to stay long euro/yen," Gong said. \par \par \uc2  "Regionals are torn between the weaker dollar and the weaker yen and, at the same time, the geopolitical uncertainties and the clouds over the global economy is making Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  underperform relative to trade-weighted baskets and the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  GROWTH PIVOTAL \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar kept to a 1.7330-1.7350 range, after failing to hold on to late-Wednesday's highs around 1.73. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won fell to 1,180, but recovered to finish local trade slightly stronger. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the upside for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was limited, given how keen their central banks are to preserve export competitiveness during these periods of uncertain global growth. \par \par \uc2  "The growth outlook is pivotal for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  going forward as a lack of upturn will see Asian central banks act to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  competitive," National Australia Bank said in a report. \par \par \uc2  "With market sentiment souring the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more real, and this is keeping both the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and Korean won from gaining against either the yen or the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We see no immediate improvement in the macro framework so by implication we continue to see Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped," the report said. \par \par \uc2  OIL IMPORTERS HEDGE \par \par \uc2  Oil prices eased from two-year highs, but traders said importers around the region were playing safe and hedging foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities. \par \par \uc2  Foreign equity investments cushioned the moves in Thailand and Korea. Foreign investors have bought a net 6.8 billion baht of Thai stocks so far in 2003, after net purchases of 14.34 billion baht in all of the previous year. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht moved in a 42.70-42.80 range. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah around 8,890 after heavy dollar buying by local importers and profit-booking by offshore speculators. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Wednesday's news that international donors have pledged $2.7 billion of fresh funding for 2003 had been discounted and so was having little impact. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was supported by exporter sales at one-month lows around 53.75, which emerged as the yen jumped off intra-day lows around 118.83. Traders said there was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dollar-buying by a government fund and the yen's weakness pushed the Taiwan dollar down in opening trade, although it pared the losses into the local close. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0810 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.25       118.33         +0.07\par   Sing dlr      1.7323       1.7325         +0.01\par   Taiwan dlr    34.658       34.644         -0.04\par   Korean won   1175.50      1176.60         +0.09\par   Baht           42.68        42.71         +0.07\par   Peso           53.66        53.68         +0.04\par   Rupiah       8881.00      8884.00         +0.03\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.25       118.74         +0.41\par   Sing dlr      1.7323       1.7341         +0.10\par   Taiwan dlr    34.658       34.753         +0.27\par   Korean won   1175.50      1185.80         +0.88\par   Baht           42.68        43.08         +0.94\par   Peso           53.66        53.38         -0.51\par   Rupiah       8881.