\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late On Yen; Peso Ignores Budget Gap \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nirmala Menon \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2003\par 11:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounced back Wednesday as the dollar succumbed to war fears, though its decline against the yen was tempered by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings from the Japanese Prime Minister. \par \par \uc2  The broadly firmer tone helped lift the Philippine peso out of the one-month troughs of the past two days as market players largely ignored record high budget deficit data for 2002, which traders said was already priced in. \par \par \uc2  In the familiar refrain heard in recent days, traders said regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remain focused on the dollar's gyrations against the yen. \par \par \uc2  But the roller coaster has left market players scratching their heads and wondering about the dollar's direction. \par \par \uc2  "The market has been very confused," declared a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, it's (dollar versus regionals) all on a soft tone, basically on the back of the dollar/yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  Hawkish remarks from the Bush administration reignited fears of an impending war in Iraq and sent the dollar plunging to Y117.00 overnight after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to Y119.15 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But in Asia Wednesday, the yen's decline was cushioned by unexpected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remarks from Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi. \par \par \uc2  Asked at the Upper House of Parliament about the yen's recent strength, Koizumi warned that "if necessary, our stance is unchanged that we will take the appropriate steps." \par \par \uc2  Though Koizumi was repeating the standard Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, it caused the dollar to briefly rally to a high of Y118.41 in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  At 0934 GMT, the dollar was quoted around Y118.36, up from Y118.04 overnight in New York. Late Tuesday in Tokyo, the dollar was at Y118.76. \par \par \uc2  For the near term, sentiment on the dollar remains bearish, especially as most of the recent economic data haven't been very encouraging, analysts said. That could lead to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players building up positions against the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was buoyed by the firmer tone of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as recent dollar demand from oil companies tapered off. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 53.675 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, down from PHP53.740 Tuesday, after ranging between PHP53.650 and PHP53.750. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Wednesday, the government announced a record 2002 budget deficit of PHP212.7 billion, or 5.3% of gross domestic product, sharply wider from PHP147 billion in 2001, but lower than the revised ceiling of PHP223 billion for 2002. \par \par \uc2  "The market had been expecting quite a bad number," said a dealer with a foreign bank, adding that it had already been priced in by the market. \par \par \uc2  In South Korea, the dollar closed at 1,176.7 won, down from KRW1,180.0 Tuesday, after trading between KRW1,173.9 and KRW1,179.8. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was confined to a tight range by importers buying at the lows and exporters selling at the highs, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank players also bought dollars on dips, providing some support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Actually, we're in a very boring market these days - just stuck within tight ranges," said Seung-hyun Kim, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  corporate sales team at BNP Paribas. "There's no fresh momentum to break through the upper or lower levels." \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar and the Thai baht tracked the yen higher amid weak market sentiment on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Near the close of the local trading session, the dollar was quoted around S$1.7322, down from S$1.7362 late Tuesday. Intraday, it traded between S$1.7300 and S$1.7345. \par \par \uc2  An uncertain outlook for the domestic economy and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the dollar from falling past the psychological S$1.7300 per U.S. dollar mark, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the dollar was quoted around THB42.73 late in Asia, down from THB42.825 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar rose in tandem with the yen, but closed off-highs as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the peak to limit its gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$34.644, down from NT$34.680 Tuesday, after trading between NT$34.590 and NT$34.702. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah closed unchanged at 8,885 per dollar amid talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar rose as high as IDR8,890 on bids from local companies looking to hedge future dollar obligations. \par \par \uc2  The market ignored reports that international donors agreed to pledge $2.7 billion in aid to Indonesia this year, though dealers said the news was positive for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030122dz1m000n3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
