\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late After Slow Start; Weak US Dlr Tone \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2003\par 09:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was stronger late Wednesday due to persistently weak market sentiment over the outlook for the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7322, down from S$1.7362 late Tuesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7300 and S$1.7345 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar kick-started the Asian session around S$1.7330 and languished around S$1.7330-40 throughout a slow morning session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Activity picked up midafternoon after the U.S. dollar staged a brief rise against the yen following comments by Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi in the country's upper house of parliament. "If necessary, our stance is unchanged that we will take the appropriate steps," Koizumi said when asked about the yen's recent strength. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ran out of steam soon after, and market participants took profit, sending the U.S. unit lower before it bounced off its intraday low of S$1.7300 against the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar seemed to be constrained in either direction against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although ongoing concerns over the possibility of a U.S.-led war with Iraq continued to pressure the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the uncertain domestic economic outlook and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept it from plummeting below the psychological S$1.7300 mark. \par \par \uc2  In London and New York trading, the U.S. dollar will continue to be supported at S$1.7300, with resistance expected at the overnight high of S$1.7365, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher as they tracked the overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys, as market participants continued to buy bonds on fears of war in the Middle East, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local bonds had opened on a positive note, and although sporadic offers were also spotted earlier, these couldn't significantly limit the gains through the session, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the yield on two-year bonds was two basis points lower at 1.06%, while the yield on five-year bonds was down eight basis points at 1.60%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was four basis points lower at 2.06%, while the yield on 10-year bonds also shed four basis points to 2.55%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds ended two basis point lower at 2.91%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swap offers mostly tracked local\par bond yields, with the two-year swap offer slipping three basis points to\par 1.21%, while the five-year offer fell four basis points to 1.94%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 10-year offer fell five basis points to 2.63%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was narrowed to 142 basis\par points, from 144 basis points late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, although the\par overnight rates slipped again. Liquidity was, however, still ample in\par the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.1875% 0.2500%   0.4375% 0.5000%\par 3-Month           0.6875% 0.8125%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 1-Year            0.8750% 1.0000%   0.8750% 1.0000%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030122dz1m000j2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
