\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Soft on yen, rupiah ignores donor meet. \b0\par\par\uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2003\par 10:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar and the\par Indonesian rupiah touched one-week lows on Tuesday as Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were weighed down by the yen's losses against other\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yen eased to its weakest since June 1999 against the\par euro and to a one-week low against the dollar in Asian trade,\par amid ongoing worries about Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Dealers said given the market seemed short of the U.S.\par dollars, amid concerns over possible war in Iraq, regionals\par were pulled down as players opted to cover those positions.\par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gyrations in particular continue to be\par determined by the ebb and flow of the broad dollar\par environment," said Sameer Goel, strategist at Bank of America.\par     He said while risks of an Iraq war are the prime strategic\par focus, the recent squaring of short dollar positions show that\par the market was also looking at "more tactical considerations".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah touched a one-week low at 8,897 per\par dollar early on, but spent most of the day in a tight\par 8,885-8,890 range, as donors to the nation met in Bali.\par     Dealers in Jakarta said some offshore players were covering\par short dollar positions and given the soft regional tone they\par could drag the rupiah to as low as 8,950 in coming sessions.\par     The market gave a muted response to comments from\par Indonesia's donors signalling their willingness to give the\par nation the $2.8 billion in aid it wanted despite a backdown on\par price hikes.\par     The price rises were part of reforms agreed with donors\par aimed at cutting state subsidies and budget deficit, but had\par triggered nationwide protests. Indonesia also said it did not\par want an extension of a $5 billion IMF loan programme that is\par scheduled to expire at the end of the year.\par     DATA PRESSURES\par     Some recent poor data added to pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such\par as Singapore dollar and the Philippine peso, dealers said.\par     The peso touched a low of 53.75 per dollar, just shy of\par Monday's one-month low of 53.76. Dealers in Manila said it was\par weighed down by Monday's news of a falling trade surplus and\par wariness before the 2002 budget deficit is released on\par Wednesday.\par     After three revisions of the deficit target, Manila hopes\par to keep last year's deficit to within 5.6 percent of gross\par domestic product, or 223 billion pesos. For this year, it aims\par to trim the deficit to 4.7 percent of GDP, or 202 billion\par pesos.\par  \par     After the close of local trade, government sources told\par Reuters the deficit would be around 213 billion pesos.\par     Singapore dollar dealers said Friday's surprisingly weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports data had reinforced fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to maintain competitiveness against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export rivals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar eased to 1.7358 per U.S. dollar, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakest since January 15, after an early test of 1.7300 - a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level some dealers suspect would now be defended by a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which has not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market for more than a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar had hit a six-month high of 1.7284 on\par Friday, before the trade data was released.\par     The Thai baht eased to 42.83 per dollar, not far from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's one-week low of 42.85. Dealers in Singapore said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales by exporters capped the baht's downside, while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most of the dollar demand was from offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar suffered its sharpest one-day decline in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par four months as the yen's losses led to stop-loss selling. It\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closed local trade at $34.68, its lowest close since early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The South Korean won                   closed local trade\par at 1,180.0 per dollar, its lowest close since January 8.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0831 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.03       118.15         -0.74\par  Sing dlr      1.7360       1.7320         -0.23\par  Taiwan dlr    34.673       34.485         -0.54\par  Korean won   1179.90      1174.10         -0.49\par  Baht           42.81        42.78         -0.07\par  Peso           53.74        53.69         -0.09\par  Rupiah       8885.00      8875.00         -0.11\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest