\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Easier on dlr bounce, data worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 886 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2003\par 04:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar\par and Taiwan dollar  fell to one-week lows and the\par Philippines peso  closed in on one-month lows on Tuesday\par as the U.S. dollar extended its rebound against the yen.\par     The U.S. dollar bounced off an early 3-=   year low against\par the euro, ahead of a knockout option at $1.0700, and was lifted\par to around 118.80 yen  on stop-loss buying.\par     Dealers said the move in the majors prompted players in\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to resume triming of short U.S. dollar\par positions, after a pause in late Asian and offshore trade.\par     They said while the dollar's upside remains checked by\par fears of a possible war in Iraq, players net short of dollars\par were looking for opportunities to cover those positions amid\par wariness of potential Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the yen.\par The yen has weakened since hitting a four-month high around\par 117.40 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said a weakening bias in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could\par also be creeping in after recent data showed some pressure on\par Asian exports.\par  \par     "We remain cautious of forming Asia longs," said Naomi\par Fink, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore.\par     "Not only due to the possibility of upcoming yen weakness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and expectations of further monetary easing,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but because of signs that exports are contracting, a clear\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par negative for the current account surplus economies of Asia,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par she added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par She said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sentiment was likely to suffer after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's surprisingly weak export numbers from Singapore and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday's sharp contraction of Philippines trade surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par POOR DATA UPS C.BANK FEARS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's exports data had reinforced fears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness against export rivals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar touched 1.7348 per U.S. dollar, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakest since January 15, as heavy offers scuttled its early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise to levels near 1.7300, beyond which dealers believe the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might come into action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Singapore dollar had hit a six-month high of 1.7284 on\par Friday, before the trade data was released.\par     Already reprimanded by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players in Taiwan took the cue from the yen's fall and sold off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar to 34.538 per U.S. dollar, its lowest level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since January 14. For a detailed report,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively on Friday to pull the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  off a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-month high of 34.401 per U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Philippine peso touched a low of 53.75 per dollar, just\par shy of one-month low of 53.76 hit on Monday.\par     Dealers in Manila said peso was weighed down by Monday's\par data showing a falling trade surplus and on wariness ahead of\par final budget deficit numbers for 2002 expected this week.\par     After three revisions of the deficit target, Manila hopes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to keep last year's deficit to within 5.6 percent of gross\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic product, or 223 billion pesos. For this year, it aims\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to trim the deficit to 4.7 percent of GDP, or 202 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pesos.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  held around 42.80 per dollar, slightly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down from late Monday and not far from Friday's one-week low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 42.85. Dealers in Singapore said dollar sales by exporters were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limiting the baht's downside, while most of the dollar demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was from offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As widely expected, the Bank of Thailand left its benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rate unchanged at 1.75 percent on Monday, saying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par robust economic growth and low inflation meant neither monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par easing nor tightening was necessary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  touched a one-week low at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,897 per dollar, as some offshore players covered their short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said comments by officials of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par International Monetary Fund and World Bank may have added to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the overall bullish sentiment on the rupiah, but they were not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading factors for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The officials said donors had an understanding attitude\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toward Indonesia's moves to reduce earlier announced rises in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fuel prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That was interpreted as suggesting Indonesia would get all\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par or most of the $2.8 billion in aid it is seeking at a two-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting of the Consultative Group on Indonesia donors, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par began on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said successful aid talks were already factored in,\par and the rupiah was only suffering technical pressure.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0246 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.72       118.15         -0.48\par  Sing dlr      1.7333       1.7320         -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    34.536       34.485         -0.15\par  Korean won   1176.30      1174.10         -0.19\par  Baht           42.76        42.78         +0.05\par  Peso           53.72        53.69         -0.06\par  Rupiah       8883.00      8875.00         -0.09\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev