\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Slightly Dn Late On MAS Fears, Dec Exports \b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2003\par 09:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar came off a new six-month high against the U.S. dollar to trade a touch weaker late Friday due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears and a worse-than-expected trade report. \par \par \uc2  At 0819 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7334, slightly up from S$1.7327 late in Asia Thursday. It traded between S$1.7292 and S$1.7339 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar kicked off the Asian session around S$1.7310 and later ticked down to S$1.7292, its lowest level since July 19, 2002. \par \par \uc2  Local banks were said to be big sellers in early trading, taking advantage of spillover bearish sentiment toward the U.S. dollar amid mounting worries over an imminent war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. dollar's retreat proved to be short-lived, as the drop below the previous psychological S$1.7300 support triggered fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering and bargain hunting soon pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to levels it closed late in Asia Thursday, thanks in part to Singapore's worse-than-expected trade performance in December. \par \par \uc2  Non-oil domestic exports, a key measurement of the trade-driven economy's health, rose 4.4% on year to S$8.0 billion in December, sharply below the average growth forecast of 13% by 10 economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  While the focus is on the U.S. dollar's bearish tone at the moment, there is also caution over any excessive strength in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of emerging markets, said a chief trader at an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to trade between S$1.7290 and S$1.7350 Monday, traders said, but added that the session could be subdued due to a public holiday in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were higher late Friday, despite mixed U.S. Treasurys overnight, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The turning point in the session was the disappointing trade data, which prompted a slew of buying after some mild selling at the open, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Lingering geopolitical concerns such as a war in Iraq also revived appetite for safe-haven products, they added. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was one basis point lower at 1.10%, while the yield on five-year bonds was down four basis points at 1.73%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was one basis point lower at 2.13%, while the yield on 10-year bonds fell one basis point to 2.59%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was three basis points lower at 2.90%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, offers were flat to lower, tracking\par local bond yields. The two-year offer fell one basis point to 1.24%,\par while the five-year swap offer was unchanged at 1.99%. The 10-year offer\par was down two basis points at 2.69%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 145 basis points\par from 146 basis points late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were unchanged to higher, but still\par hovering near their recent lows as liquidity remained flush in the\par banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late    Friday    Late    Thursday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.3750% 0.5000%   0.2500% 0.3750%\par 3-Month           0.6875% 0.8125%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 1-Year            0.8750% 1.0000%   0.8750% 1.0000%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Shen Hong, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4156;\par hong.shen@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030117dz1h000id\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\